(gen_random_uuid(), 'aps-jobs-australia-20261127', 'australia', 'Australia',
'APS Jobs Australia: DFAT Roles Pay $102,266 to $114,988',
'APS Jobs Australia: DFAT Roles Pay $102,266 to $114,988',
'APS jobs Australia include DFAT APS6 Enabling Services roles in Canberra at $102,266 to $114,988 a year plus super, closing 29 November 2026.',
'APS jobs Australia include DFAT APS6 Enabling Services roles in Canberra at $102,266 to $114,988 a year plus super, closing 29 November 2026.',
$$<p>The Australian Public Service is hiring in Canberra, with the Department of Foreign Affairs and Trade advertising multiple APS6 roles. APS jobs Australia in this roundup pay from $82,336 to $118,084 a year plus superannuation, and the headline DFAT roles close on 29 November 2026.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>Australian Public Service: Department of Foreign Affairs and Trade and Department of Infrastructure, Transport, Regional Development, Communications, Sport and the Arts</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>APS6 Enabling Services (multiple vacancies), APS6 Cyber Security Analyst, APS5 and APS6 Compliance Officers</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$82,336 to $118,084 a year, plus 15.4 percent superannuation</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>DFAT APS6 roles close 11:30pm ADST on Sunday 29 November 2026; the Cyber Security Analyst closed 22 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through the departmental careers site</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Varies by role; relevant professional experience for APS6 posts</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Application and merit assessment; a merit pool may be formed for future similar vacancies</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What APS jobs Australia involve</h2><p>The Department of Foreign Affairs and Trade is hiring multiple APS6 Enabling Services staff in Canberra, on ongoing or non-ongoing terms, at $102,266 to $114,988 a year plus 15.4 percent employer superannuation. The roles include affirmative measures streams for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander applicants and for people with disability. The Cyber Security Analyst role, at APS6 level with the Department of Infrastructure, covered strategy, architecture and cyber security in Canberra, Brisbane, Sydney and Melbourne, at $99,733 to $118,084 a year plus 15.4 percent superannuation, with flexible and hybrid working. Recruitment agencies are also advertising APS5 Compliance Officers at $82,336 to $90,234 and APS6 Senior Compliance Officers at $91,140 to $102,152, on 12-month placements in Canberra and Melbourne. Readers looking more widely can browse <a href="https://growentix.cloud/australia">Australia jobs</a> and our guide to <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/australia-aps-jobs-november-2026-20261121">Australia APS jobs in November 2026</a>.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p>APS roles are open to Australian citizens and applicants must satisfy the relevant security and eligibility requirements. The DFAT affirmative measures streams are open only to Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander applicants or only to people with disability (under s 33 of the Australian Public Service Commissioner's Directions 2022). A merit pool may be established from the DFAT process and used to fill future similar vacancies in Canberra and other locations in the same metropolitan area.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p> DFAT APS6 Enabling Services roles are $102,266 to $114,988 pa plus 15.4% employer super. The Cyber Security Analyst role is $99,733 to $118,084 pa plus 15.4% super. Agency advertised Compliance Officers are $82,336 to $90,234 pa at APS5 and $91,140 to $102,152 pa at APS6 plus super. All APS roles come with the standard Australian Public Service benefits (super, annual leave and flexible working).</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply via the hiring department's careers site or via the recruitment agency for the compliance placements. The DFAT APS6 Enabling Services applications close at 11:30 pm Australian Eastern Daylight Time on Sunday 29 November 2026. The Cyber Security Analyst application closed at 11:59 pm Australian Eastern Daylight Time on Sunday 22 November 2026 so please check the live departmental site for the current equivalent opportunities.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The listings do not say how many posts are available in the DFAT process beyond describing them as multiple vacancies, and they give no interview dates or start dates. The compliance officer roles are agency placements rather than direct APS appointments, and the listings checked do not name their exact department is not named in the listings checked. None of the listings state whether visa sponsorship is available, and APS roles normally require Australian citizenship, so international applicants should check the individual advert before applying.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> APS applications are free and no department will ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://indigcareers.com.au/en-us/Ads/Job/ArtMID/608/ArticleID/7051/APS6-Enabling-Services-including-Affirmative-Measures-Multiple-Vacancies">IndigCareers</a> (the DFAT APS6 Enabling Services listing: salary, closing date and affirmative measures); <a href="https://au.jora.com/job/APS6-Enabling-Services-ac4f2c84e128d43cca76ce54004f6ee1?abstract_type=extended_llm&disallow=true&fsv=true&sl=Garran+ACT&sol_key=73ef354751f1275547b5c6b02e151c59&sp=serp&sponsored=false&sq=Consulate&sr=2&tk=Xs1X8ZSz3x39H7nj1VY7-GNcYIWEWrT_93YuaGlH5&trigger_source=serp">Jora</a> (the DFAT APS6 Enabling Services listing reproduced: salary and closing date); <a href="https://career10.successfactors.com/career?career%5fns=job%5flisting&company=DoIT&navBarLevel=JOB%5fSEARCH&rcm%5fsite%5flocale=en%5fGB&career_job_req_id=48318&selected_lang=en_GB&jobAlertController_jobAlertId=&jobAlertController_jobAlertName=&browserTimeZone=Europe/Kiev&_s.crb=5F8X%2f5zB5DfsxbhtNAl7KLKhVqAIkH%2fcngnOY5bT0c4%3d">SuccessFactors</a> (the APS6 Cyber Security Analyst listing: salary, locations and closing date).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>When do the DFAT APS6 roles close?</h3><p>At 11.30pm Australian Eastern Daylight Time on Sunday 29 November 2026.</p><h3>How much do the DFAT APS6 roles pay?</h3><p>$102,266 to $114,988 per annum plus 15.4% employer super.</p><h3>What are affirmative measures roles?</h3><p>They are APS vacancies open only to a specified group (e.g. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people or people with a disability) pursuant to the Public Service Commissioner's Directions.</p><h3>Do I need to be an Australian citizen?</h3><p>APS roles generally require Australian citizenship so applicants should check the individual advertisement.</p>
$$,
