-- government-of-canada-jobs-20261127 (canada; Canada; verifiedAt 2026-11-27)
INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt", "verifiedAt", "authorName")
VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'government-of-canada-jobs-20261127', 'canada', 'Canada',
'Government of Canada Jobs: Six Roles Pay Up to $97,266',
'Government of Canada Jobs: Six Roles Pay Up to $97,266',
'Government of Canada jobs are open through GC Jobs, with Correctional Officer I at $77,510 to $97,266 a year across 24 locations, closing 31 December 2026.',
'Government of Canada jobs are open through GC Jobs, with Correctional Officer I at $77,510 to $97,266 a year across 24 locations, closing 31 December 2026.',
$$<p>The Government of Canada is hiring across several departments, with six federal recruitment processes open in November 2026. Government of Canada jobs in this roundup pay from $27.47 an hour to $114,404 a year, and the latest closing date is 31 December 2026.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>Government of Canada: Correctional Service Canada, Parks Canada, Canadian Grain Commission, Transport Canada, National Defence and Canadian Coast Guard</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Correctional Officer I, Grain Inspector Trainee, Visitor Services Attendant II, General Maintenance Worker, Regional Railway Inspector, Administration Officer</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$27.47 to $33.95 an hour, or $57,328 to $114,404 a year, depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Closing 29 November to 31 December 2026 depending on the role, at 11:59pm Pacific Time</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through GC Jobs, the Public Service Resourcing System</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Varies by role; no previous grain inspection experience needed for the trainee posts</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Online application, assessment and security clearance; some processes build candidate pools for future vacancies</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What government of Canada jobs involve</h2><p>Correctional Service Canada is recruiting Correctional Officer I's at 24 sites across eight provinces, at $77,510 to $97,266/year, closing 31 Dec 2026. The Canadian Grain Commission is hiring Grain Inspector Trainees in Western Canada (closing 14 Dec 2026) and in Eastern Canada (closing 31 Dec 2026) at $57,328 to $68,147/year, with no previous professional grain inspection experience required. Parks Canada is looking for Visitor Services Attendant II's in Cape Breton Highlands, NS at $27.47 to $29.85/hour, closing 10 Dec 2026. Correctional Service Canada is also seeking General Maintenance Workers at the healing lodges in the Prairies at $31.24 to $33.95/hour, closing 15 Dec 2026. Transport Canada is recruiting a Regional Railway Inspector in Thunder Bay, Ontario at $97,453 to $114,404, closing 29 Nov 2026. For a wider range of opportunities, readers can check out <a href="https://growentix.cloud/canada">Canada jobs</a> and our guide to <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/correctional-officer-jobs-canada-24-locations-20261116">correctional officer jobs in Canada</a>.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p>The majority of these processes are open to people residing in Canada as well as Canadian citizens and permanent residents overseas. The Grain Inspector Trainee position is an entry point into a technical government career. The Correctional Officer and Railway Inspector positions require relevant experience (and for the Correctional Officer role a second application stage on the department's recruitment site following the GC Jobs application). Some of the processes are in fact inventories or candidate pools rather than actual vacancies so applying does not necessarily lead to an immediate appointment. Security clearance is required for a number of the roles.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p> Regional Railway Inspector: $97,453 - $114,404; Correctional Officer I: $77,510 - $97,266; Grain Inspector Trainee: $57,328 - $68,147; Administration Officer (National Defence and Canadian Coast Guard): $61,786 - $69,106. General Maintenance Worker: $31.24 to $33.95 an hour, and the Visitor Services Attendant II: $27.47 - $29.85/hr (that rate was under review). All federal positions come with Government of Canada benefits (health, pension and paid leave).</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply online via GC Jobs by creating an account in the Public Service Resourcing System. All six postings close at 11.59pm PT on their respective deadlines: Railway Inspector (29 Nov 2026), Visitor Services Attendant (10 Dec), Western Grain Inspector Trainee (14 Dec), General Maintenance Worker (15 Dec) and Eastern Grain Inspector Trainee/Correctional Officer (31 Dec 2026). The Administration Officer posting closed on 20 Nov 2026. Correctional Officer applicants will also be required to complete the follow-up stage on the department's recruitment platform.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The listings don't indicate how many positions are available in each process, nor do they list any interview dates or start dates. A number of the processes are pools for current and future vacancies so your application may not result in a position being offered immediately. The Visitor Services Attendant salary was listed as under review so the live GC Jobs listing is the one to go by. None of the listings state whether visa sponsorship is available for applicants from outside of Canada.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> Government of Canada applications are free and no department will ever ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://www.tcf-fca.ca/6-new-government-of-canada-jobs-november-2026/">TCF-FCA</a> (the six November 2026 federal processes: salaries, locations and deadlines); <a href="https://immigrationnewscanada.ca/government-of-canada-jobs-november-2026/">Immigration News Canada</a> (the same six processes: deadlines, pay and application links); <a href="https://www.gjobs.ca/jobs/2482163">GJobs</a> (the Transport Canada Regional Railway Inspector posting as reproduced: salary, location and closing date).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What's the highest paid Government of Canada position in here?</h3><p>The Regional Railway Inspector at $97,453 to $114,404 a year.</p><h3>When do these roles close?</h3><p>From 29 November to 31 December 2026 at 11.59pm Pacific Time.</p><h3>Are all of these immediate posts?</h3><p>No, several are inventories or candidate pools that the departments can draw on to fill current and future roles.</p><h3>Where do I apply?</h3><p>Online via GC Jobs, the Public Service Resourcing System.</p>
$$,
$$<p>The Government of Canada is hiring across several departments, with six federal recruitment processes open in November 2026. Government of Canada jobs in this roundup pay from $27.47 an hour to $114,404 a year, and the latest closing date is 31 December 2026.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>Government of Canada: Correctional Service Canada, Parks Canada, Canadian Grain Commission, Transport Canada, National Defence and Canadian Coast Guard</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Correctional Officer I, Grain Inspector Trainee, Visitor Services Attendant II, General Maintenance Worker, Regional Railway Inspector, Administration Officer</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$27.47 to $33.95 an hour, or $57,328 to $114,404 a year, depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Closing 29 November to 31 December 2026 depending on the role, at 11:59pm Pacific Time</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through GC Jobs, the Public Service Resourcing System</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Varies by role; no previous grain inspection experience needed for the trainee posts</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Online application, assessment and security clearance; some processes build candidate pools for future vacancies</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What government of Canada jobs involve</h2><p>Correctional Service Canada is recruiting Correctional Officer I's at 24 sites across eight provinces, at $77,510 to $97,266/year, closing 31 Dec 2026. The Canadian Grain Commission is hiring Grain Inspector Trainees in Western Canada (closing 14 Dec 2026) and in Eastern Canada (closing 31 Dec 2026) at $57,328 to $68,147/year, with no previous professional grain inspection experience required. Parks Canada is looking for Visitor Services Attendant II's in Cape Breton Highlands, NS at $27.47 to $29.85/hour, closing 10 Dec 2026. Correctional Service Canada is also seeking General Maintenance Workers at the healing lodges in the Prairies at $31.24 to $33.95/hour, closing 15 Dec 2026. Transport Canada is recruiting a Regional Railway Inspector in Thunder Bay, Ontario at $97,453 to $114,404, closing 29 Nov 2026. For a wider range of opportunities, readers can check out <a href="https://growentix.cloud/canada">Canada jobs</a> and our guide to <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/correctional-officer-jobs-canada-24-locations-20261116">correctional officer jobs in Canada</a>.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p>The majority of these processes are open to people residing in Canada as well as Canadian citizens and permanent residents overseas. The Grain Inspector Trainee position is an entry point into a technical government career. The Correctional Officer and Railway Inspector positions require relevant experience (and for the Correctional Officer role a second application stage on the department's recruitment site following the GC Jobs application). Some of the processes are in fact inventories or candidate pools rather than actual vacancies so applying does not necessarily lead to an immediate appointment. Security clearance is required for a number of the roles.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p> Regional Railway Inspector: $97,453 - $114,404; Correctional Officer I: $77,510 - $97,266; Grain Inspector Trainee: $57,328 - $68,147; Administration Officer (National Defence and Canadian Coast Guard): $61,786 - $69,106. General Maintenance Worker: $31.24 to $33.95 an hour, and the Visitor Services Attendant II: $27.47 - $29.85/hr (that rate was under review). All federal positions come with Government of Canada benefits (health, pension and paid leave).</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply online via GC Jobs by creating an account in the Public Service Resourcing System. All six postings close at 11.59pm PT on their respective deadlines: Railway Inspector (29 Nov 2026), Visitor Services Attendant (10 Dec), Western Grain Inspector Trainee (14 Dec), General Maintenance Worker (15 Dec) and Eastern Grain Inspector Trainee/Correctional Officer (31 Dec 2026). The Administration Officer posting closed on 20 Nov 2026. Correctional Officer applicants will also be required to complete the follow-up stage on the department's recruitment platform.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The listings don't indicate how many positions are available in each process, nor do they list any interview dates or start dates. A number of the processes are pools for current and future vacancies so your application may not result in a position being offered immediately. The Visitor Services Attendant salary was listed as under review so the live GC Jobs listing is the one to go by. None of the listings state whether visa sponsorship is available for applicants from outside of Canada.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> Government of Canada applications are free and no department will ever ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://www.tcf-fca.ca/6-new-government-of-canada-jobs-november-2026/">TCF-FCA</a> (the six November 2026 federal processes: salaries, locations and deadlines); <a href="https://immigrationnewscanada.ca/government-of-canada-jobs-november-2026/">Immigration News Canada</a> (the same six processes: deadlines, pay and application links); <a href="https://www.gjobs.ca/jobs/2482163">GJobs</a> (the Transport Canada Regional Railway Inspector posting as reproduced: salary, location and closing date).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What's the highest paid Government of Canada position in here?</h3><p>The Regional Railway Inspector at $97,453 to $114,404 a year.</p><h3>When do these roles close?</h3><p>From 29 November to 31 December 2026 at 11.59pm Pacific Time.</p><h3>Are all of these immediate posts?</h3><p>No, several are inventories or candidate pools that the departments can draw on to fill current and future roles.</p><h3>Where do I apply?</h3><p>Online via GC Jobs, the Public Service Resourcing System.</p>
