(gen_random_uuid(), 'jobs-in-boston-usa-20261127', 'usa', 'USA',
'Jobs in Boston USA: State Roles Pay Up to $131,826',
'Jobs in Boston USA: State Roles Pay Up to $131,826',
'Jobs in Boston USA include a Massachusetts Digital Evidence Analyst at $87,930 and a federal Administrative Operations Supervisor at $67,652 to $131,826.',
'Jobs in Boston USA include a Massachusetts Digital Evidence Analyst at $87,930 and a federal Administrative Operations Supervisor at $67,652 to $131,826.',
$$<p>Massachusetts state government and the federal courts are hiring in Boston, with digital forensics, project management and court administration roles open. Jobs in Boston USA in this roundup pay from $67,652 to $131,826 a year, though one headline deadline has already passed.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>Commonwealth of Massachusetts and US District Court, District of Massachusetts</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Digital Evidence Analyst I, Administrative Operations Supervisor, Project Manager, Forest and Park Supervisor II, Seasonal Office Support Specialist II</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$67,652 to $131,826 a year, depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Digital Evidence Analyst closed 24 November 2026; Administrative Operations Supervisor open until filled; Project Manager first consideration within 14 days of 28 October 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through the Massachusetts Attorney General employment portal and the court recruitment system</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Two to four years of digital forensics experience for the analyst role; five years of planning experience for the Project Manager</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Application and assessment; the Attorney General's Office warns that applications through MassCareers are not received</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What jobs in Boston USA involve</h2><p>The Digital Evidence Analyst I works in the Attorney General's Digital Evidence Laboratory in Boston, collecting and analysing mobile devices, computers, media and data from networks and third-party providers, on a hybrid model with some remote workdays. The Administrative Operations Supervisor in the US Probation and Pretrial Services Office supervises day-to-day support functions in the Boston office and directs the work of clerks and other staff. The Division of Capital Asset Management and Maintenance needs a Project Manager to oversee property dispositions, particularly in support of the State Land for Homes Initiative. Seasonal roles include a Forest and Park Supervisor II at Roxbury Heritage State Park and an Office Support Specialist II in finance. Readers looking more widely can browse <a href="https://growentix.cloud/usa">USA jobs</a> and our guide to <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/software-engineer-jobs-in-usa-for-foreigners-h-1b-pay-and-hiring-guide-20261029">software engineer jobs in the USA for foreigners</a>.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p>The Digital Evidence Analyst needs two to four years of experience in digital forensics. The Project Manager needs at least five years of full-time technical or professional experience in urban, regional, environmental or land use planning, including three years in a professional capacity and one year in a supervisory capacity. The Administrative Operations Supervisor role suits an experienced administrator with knowledge of probation and pretrial services business operations. The seasonal park supervisor needs three years of experience in forestry, parks or recreational management, including one year in a supervisory capacity. The listings do not state any nationality restriction, but applicants must be authorised to work in the United States.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p>The Digital Evidence Analyst I pays $87,930 a year. The Administrative Operations Supervisor pays $67,652 to $131,826, depending on qualifications and experience, at classification level CL-27-28. The Project Manager and seasonal roles give no salary figure in the listings checked. State roles carry Massachusetts employee benefits, and federal court roles carry federal benefits.</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>The Digital Evidence Analyst application closed on 24 November 2026 at 5 pm Eastern Time, and applications had to go through the Attorney General's Office employment portal at mass.gov/ago/employment, not through MassCareers, which does not forward applications to that office. The Administrative Operations Supervisor is open until filled through the court's online applicant tracking system. The Project Manager gave first consideration to applicants who applied within the first 14 days of its 28 October 2026 posting, so readers should check the live MassCareers listing before applying.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The listings don't state how many posts there are for each role and give no interview dates or start dates. The Project Manager and the seasonal posts don't state a salary in the versions we checked. None of the listings indicate whether visa sponsorship is available so international applicants should check directly with the agency before applying.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> MA state and federal court applications are free and no agency will ever ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://www.onetonline.org/link/jobinfo?id=C7EAF1C17B41408A9FCE2220D70B7996206">O*NET OnLine</a> (the Massachusetts Digital Evidence Analyst listing: salary, deadline and application route); <a href="https://www.map.uscourts.gov/sites/map/files/Vacancy%2026-05_Adminitrative%20Operations%20Supervisor_Re-Opened2026.pdf">US Courts</a> (the Administrative Operations Supervisor vacancy notice: salary, location and open-until-filled status); <a href="https://www.onetonline.org/link/jobinfo?id=F4A245C086D34396A44F64675084BEB0206">O*NET OnLine</a> (the DCAMM Project Manager listing: duties and experience requirements).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Is the Boston Digital Evidence Analyst role still open?</h3><p>No, the application deadline was 24th November 2026 at 5pm Eastern Time.</p><h3>How do I go about applying for the Attorney General posts?</h3><p>Apply directly via the Attorney General's Office employment portal at mass.gov/ago/employment. Applications submitted via MassCareers will not be accepted.</p><h3>What's the highest paying Boston role in this list?</h3><p>The Administrative Operations Supervisor at $67,652 to $131,826 per annum.</p><h3>Is the court role open until filled?</h3><p>Yes, the Administrative Operations Supervisor vacancy is open until filled.</p>
$$,
