(gen_random_uuid(), 'jobs-in-dallas-usa-20261127', 'usa', 'USA',
'Jobs in Dallas USA: City Roles Pay Up to $111,800',
'Jobs in Dallas USA: City Roles Pay Up to $111,800',
'Jobs in Dallas USA are open with the City of Dallas, including a Senior IT Project Manager at $89,440 to $111,800 a year, closing 16 December 2026.',
'Jobs in Dallas USA are open with the City of Dallas, including a Senior IT Project Manager at $89,440 to $111,800 a year, closing 16 December 2026.',
$$<p>The City of Dallas is hiring throughout its various departments (technology, planning, City Attorney's Office etc). Jobs in Dallas USA in this roundup pay from $44,720 to $111,800 a year, and the earliest closing dates fall in late November 2026.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>City of Dallas</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Senior Information Technology Project Manager, Assistant City Attorney, Planner II, Project Coordinator, Inspector III, Customer Service Representative I, Welder, Manager - Forensics</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$44,720 to $111,800 a year, depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Senior IT Project Manager closes 16 December 2026; Assistant City Attorney recruitment runs 23 November to 24 December 2026; planning roles close 20 November to 2 December 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through the City of Dallas careers portal</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Five years of relevant experience for the Assistant City Attorney; high school diploma or GED for the Customer Service Representative; one year of welding experience for the Welder</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Application and assessment; civil service rules apply to civil service posts</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What jobs in Dallas USA involve</h2><p>The headline role is Senior Information Technology Project Manager in Information Technology Services, managing technology projects for city vehicles and mobile devices, at $89,440 to $111,800 a year. The City Attorney's Office needs an Assistant City Attorney in Economic and Community Development, for an attorney with at least five years of relevant experience. Planning and Development is hiring Planner II posts in urban design, zoning and the Q-Team, plus Project Coordinators and a multidisciplinary Inspector III in plumbing. Other open roles include a Customer Service Representative in Vital Statistics at $21.50 to $21.78 an hour, a Welder in Parks and Recreation at $21.67 to $23.60 an hour, and a Manager - Forensics with Dallas Police at $73,590 to $91,978 a year. Readers looking more widely can browse <a href="https://growentix.cloud/usa">USA jobs</a> and our guide to <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/truck-driver-jobs-in-usa-salary-cdl-pay-per-mile-visa-routes-20261026">truck driver jobs in the USA</a>, another large Texas employer route.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p>The Senior IT Project Manager role suits an experienced technology project manager, and the Assistant City Attorney needs at least five years of relevant legal experience. The Customer Service Representative needs only a high school diploma or GED, the Welder needs one year of welding experience, and the planning roles suit qualified planners. The listings do not state any nationality restriction, but applicants must be authorised to work in the United States.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p>Pay varies considerably by role. Senior IT Project Manager pays $89,440 to $111,800 a year, the Manager - Forensics pays $73,590 to $91,978, and the Customer Service Representative is $44,720-$45,302/year ($21.50-$21.78/hour), Welder is $21.67-$23.60/hour. No salary is given for the Assistant City Attorney or the planning roles give no salary figure in the listings checked. City roles come with City of Dallas benefits (health, retirement and paid leave).</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply via the City of Dallas careers site, searching for the role title. The Senior IT Project Manager closes 16th December 2026, the Assistant City Attorney is open from 23rd November to 24th December 2026 and the planning roles close 20th November to 2nd December 2026 so one of those may already be closed by the time you get to it. The Customer Service Representative position closed 26th November 2026.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The listings don't specify how many posts there are for each role, nor do they give any interview dates or start dates. The Assistant City Attorney and Planning listings give no salary in the versions we checked. None of the listings indicate whether visa sponsorship is available so international applicants should check directly with the City of Dallas prior to applying.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> City of Dallas applications are free and no city department will ever ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://app.joinhandshake.com/public/jobs/11986070">Handshake</a> (the City of Dallas Senior IT Project Manager listing: salary and closing date); <a href="https://jobera.com/job/dallascityhall-senior-information-technology-project-manager-information-technology-service-civil-service-7c811f98/">Jobera</a> (the same role reproduced: salary and posting date); <a href="https://careerservices.alcorn.edu/jobs/dallas-city-attorney-office-assistant-city-attorney-economic-and-community-development-2/">Alcorn State University</a> (the Assistant City Attorney listing: recruitment dates and experience requirement).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What's the highest paid role in Dallas in this list?</h3><p>The Senior Information Technology Project Manager at $89,440 to $111,800 per annum.</p><h3>When does the Senior IT Project Manager post close?</h3><p>On 16 December 2026.</p><h3>Are there any entry level Dallas city roles?</h3><p>Yes, the Customer Service Representative role only requires a high school diploma or GED and the Welder role requires one year of welding experience.</p><h3>Where do I apply?</h3><p>Online via the City of Dallas careers site.</p>
$$,
$$<p>The City of Dallas is hiring throughout its various departments (technology, planning, City Attorney's Office etc). Jobs in Dallas USA in this roundup pay from $44,720 to $111,800 a year, and the earliest closing dates fall in late November 2026.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>City of Dallas</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Senior Information Technology Project Manager, Assistant City Attorney, Planner II, Project Coordinator, Inspector III, Customer Service Representative I, Welder, Manager - Forensics</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$44,720 to $111,800 a year, depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Senior IT Project Manager closes 16 December 2026; Assistant City Attorney recruitment runs 23 November to 24 December 2026; planning roles close 20 November to 2 December 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through the City of Dallas careers portal</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Five years of relevant experience for the Assistant City Attorney; high school diploma or GED for the Customer Service Representative; one year of welding experience for the Welder</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Application and assessment; civil service rules apply to civil service posts</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What jobs in Dallas USA involve</h2><p>The headline role is Senior Information Technology Project Manager in Information Technology Services, managing technology projects for city vehicles and mobile devices, at $89,440 to $111,800 a year. The City Attorney's Office needs an Assistant City Attorney in Economic and Community Development, for an attorney with at least five years of relevant experience. Planning and Development is hiring Planner II posts in urban design, zoning and the Q-Team, plus Project Coordinators and a multidisciplinary Inspector III in plumbing. Other open roles include a Customer Service Representative in Vital Statistics at $21.50 to $21.78 an hour, a Welder in Parks and Recreation at $21.6