ing listings give no salary in the versions we checked. None of the listings indicate whether visa sponsorship is available so international applicants should check directly with the City of Dallas prior to applying.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> City of Dallas applications are free and no city department will ever ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://app.joinhandshake.com/public/jobs/11986070">Handshake</a> (the City of Dallas Senior IT Project Manager listing: salary and closing date); <a href="https://jobera.com/job/dallascityhall-senior-information-technology-project-manager-information-technology-service-civil-service-7c811f98/">Jobera</a> (the same role reproduced: salary and posting date); <a href="https://careerservices.alcorn.edu/jobs/dallas-city-attorney-office-assistant-city-attorney-economic-and-community-development-2/">Alcorn State University</a> (the Assistant City Attorney listing: recruitment dates and experience requirement).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What's the highest paid role in Dallas in this list?</h3><p>The Senior Information Technology Project Manager at $89,440 to $111,800 per annum.</p><h3>When does the Senior IT Project Manager post close?</h3><p>On 16 December 2026.</p><h3>Are there any entry level Dallas city roles?</h3><p>Yes, the Customer Service Representative role only requires a high school diploma or GED and the Welder role requires one year of welding experience.</p><h3>Where do I apply?</h3><p>Online via the City of Dallas careers site.</p>
