-- jobs-in-georgia-usa-20261127 (usa; USA; verifiedAt 2026-11-27)
INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt", "verifiedAt", "authorName")
VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'jobs-in-georgia-usa-20261127', 'usa', 'USA',
'Jobs in Georgia USA: State Roles Pay $32,000 to $72,000',
'Jobs in Georgia USA: State Roles Pay $32,000 to $72,000',
'Jobs in Georgia USA are open with the State of Georgia, including a Junior Systems Analyst at $62,000 to $72,000 and an Administrative Services Associate.',
'Jobs in Georgia USA are open with the State of Georgia, including a Junior Systems Analyst at $62,000 to $72,000 and an Administrative Services Associate.',
$$<p>The State of Georgia is recruiting in Atlanta and throughout the state in the areas of administration, systems, procurement and driver services. Jobs in Georgia USA in this roundup pay from $32,000 to $72,000 a year, and applications go in through Team Georgia Careers.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>State of Georgia, various agencies</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Junior Systems Analyst, Contract Management 1, Administrative Services Associate, Purchasing Assistant 2, Identity and Driver Credential Specialist 1</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$32,000 to $72,000 a year, depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Administrative Services Associate closes 3 December 2026; Purchasing Assistant 2 closed 24 November 2026; other posts may close once a suitable pool is found</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through Team Georgia Careers at careers.georgia.gov</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>High school diploma or GED plus two years of relevant experience for the Purchasing Assistant; degree-level systems work for the Junior Systems Analyst</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Online application and assessment; postings may close early once a suitable applicant pool is identified</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What jobs in Georgia USA involve</h2><p>The Junior Systems Analyst, with the Judicial Council and Administrative Office of the Courts in Atlanta, supports the statewide Court Management System by gathering requirements, analysing workflows and documenting system functions, with regular office attendance and statewide travel. The Contract Management 1 post with the Department of Administrative Services is an entry-level procurement role on a hybrid team that encourages telework, with some days in the office. The Administrative Services Associate with the Department of Public Health provides administrative support in Atlanta, and the Identity and Driver Credential Specialist 1 with the Department of Driver Services in Statesboro helps residents with driving credentials. The Purchasing Assistant 2 with the Department of Public Safety works in supply at headquarters in Atlanta. Readers looking more widely can browse <a href="https://growentix.cloud/usa">USA jobs</a> and our guide to <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/security-guard-jobs-in-usa-requirements-licence-and-pay-guide-20261031">security guard jobs in the USA</a>.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p>The Purchasing Assistant needs a high school diploma or GED and two years of job-related experience in inventory, purchasing or supply chain management, or one year at the lower Purchasing Agent 1 level. The Junior Systems Analyst suits a systems analyst with court or public-sector experience, and the Contract Management post is described as an entry-level role for an innovative thinker who enjoys a fast-paced environment. The listings do not state any nationality restriction, but applicants must be authorised to work in the United States.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p>The Junior Systems Analyst pays $62,000 to $72,000 a year, the Contract Management 1 post pays $44,000 to $54,000, the Administrative Services Associate pays $33,042 to $40,560, the Purchasing Assistant 2 pays $40,000, and the Identity and Driver Credential Specialist 1 pays $32,000 a year, non-negotiable. State roles carry Georgia state employee benefits, including health coverage, retirement and paid leave.</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply online via Team Georgia Careers at careers.georgia.gov (current state employees apply via the GA@WORK Jobs Hub). The Administrative Services Associate closes 3 Dec 2026 and the Purchasing Assistant 2 closed 24 Nov 2026. A number of the Georgia postings state that they may close at any time once a sufficient applicant pool has been identified so applicants are advised to apply early rather than wait for a closing date.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The postings don't state how many posts there are for each role and give no interview dates or start dates. The Junior Systems Analyst and Contract Management postings give no closure date in the versions we checked. None of the postings state whether visa sponsorship is available so international applicants should check directly with the agency before applying.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> State of Georgia applications are free and no State agency will ever ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://dps.georgia.gov/purchasing-asst-2-supply-headquarters-atlanta">Georgia Department of Public Safety</a> (Purchasing Assistant 2 vacancy: salary, qualifications and deadline); <a href="https://careers.workupcoweta.com/companies/georgia-gov/jobs/100600123-junior-systems-analyst">WorkUp Coweta</a> (Junior Systems Analyst listing reproduced from Georgia.gov: salary and duties); <a href="https://careers.workupcoweta.com/companies/georgia-gov/jobs/100457413-contract-management-1">WorkUp Coweta</a> (Contract Management 1 listing reproduced from Georgia.gov: salary and hybrid working).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What's the highest paid role in Georgia in this list?</h3><p>The Junior Systems Analyst, at $62,000 to $72,000 a year.</p><h3>When does the Administrative Services Associate position close?</h3><p>On 3 December 2026.</p><h3>Where do I apply for Georgia state jobs?</h3><p>Online via Team Georgia Careers at careers.georgia.gov</p><h3>Can postings close early?</h3><p>Yes, several Georgia postings state they may close at any time once they have identified a satisfactory applicant pool.</p>
$$,
