-- jobs-in-germany-20261127 (europe; Germany; verifiedAt 2026-11-27)
INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt", "verifiedAt", "authorName")
VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'jobs-in-germany-20261127', 'europe', 'Germany',
'Jobs in Germany: Skilled Roles Listed on Make it in Germany',
'Jobs in Germany: Skilled Roles Listed on Make it in Germany',
'Jobs in Germany are listed on Make it in Germany, with 174 training and skilled vacancies posted in late November 2026, including engineers and electricians.',
'Jobs in Germany are listed on Make it in Germany, with 174 training and skilled vacancies posted in late November 2026, including engineers and electricians.',
$$<p>Germany's official 'Make it in Germany' job exchange is listing skilled and training vacancies throughout the country, with new vacancies added in late November 2026. Jobs in Germany in this roundup cover engineers, electricians, mechanics, cooks and chefs, and applications go in through the employer's own listing on the exchange.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>Make it in Germany job exchange, Federal Government of Germany; employers include BMW, Rolls-Royce Deutschland, Michelin, TU Bergakademie Freiberg and Dussmann Service</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Requirement-Manager, Electronics Technician, Engineer - Mechanical Engineering, Aircraft Mechanic, Chef, Cook, Industrial Engineer, Mechatronics Technician, Electrician</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Roles posted 1 to 25 November 2026; no closing dates stated on the listings checked</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through the Make it in Germany job listings, then to the employer's own application page</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Varies by role; recognised vocational qualification or engineering degree for the skilled posts</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Application to the employer; skilled-worker visa rules apply to applicants from outside the EU</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What jobs in Germany involve</h2><p>The latest salaried posts are a Requirement Manager (software engineering) in Nurnberg (23/25 Nov 2026), an Electronics Technician in operating technology with Wellpappe Alzenau (23 Nov 2026), and an Engineer in Mechanical Engineering with TU Bergakademie Freiberg (24 Nov 2026). A Chef post with Dussmann Service in Berlin and an Industrial Engineer post with Saarland University in Saarbrucken were both posted on 25 Nov 2026. Training posts include an Aircraft Mechanic apprenticeship with EXTRA Aircraft Maintenance in Hunxe, a two wheel mechatronics technician trainee with BMW in Bonn and a Process Mechanic with REHAU Industries in Velen (all 25 Nov 2026). There are also a number of skilled posts available in the form of electricians, mechatronics technicians, machine and plant operators, cooks and meat cutters. For those wanting to look more widely, there's <a href="https://growentix.cloud/europe">Europe jobs</a> and our guide to <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/germany-skilled-worker-jobs-2026-20261121">Germany skilled worker jobs in 2026</a>.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p>These are posts open to those with the relevant vocational qualification or degree and many are for skilled workers from outside Germany. Doctors, nurses, engineers, IT specialists, scientists, craft workers, transport workers and green jobs are listed as in-demand professions on Make it in Germany. Applicants from outside the EU will generally need to have a recognised qualification and in most cases a job offer prior to applying for a skilled worker visa. The employer will often require German language ability is often required by the employer.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p>The Make it in Germany listings provide no salary information so no salary is claimed here. The employer determines the German skilled worker rate and the sector rate under the collective agreement and that figure will be on the individual employer's listing or in the job offer. Applicants should check the live listing for the salary, hours and contract type prior to applying.</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply via the Make it in Germany job board, open the role and follow the link to the employer's own application page. The exchange has 174 training posts in the latest view, 49 salaried posts in one filtered view and 68 in another so it's worth filtering by occupation, region and type of job. There are no closing dates on the posts that have been checked and posts are removed as soon as they're filled so it's advisable to apply early.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The listings don't state the salaries, the closing dates, the post counts, the interview dates or the start dates in the versions we checked. They don't state the required German language level for each post and they don't state whether the employer will support a visa application so applicants should check the individual employer's advert before applying.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> It's free on the German listings and no employer will ever ask you to pay anything in exchange for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://www.make-it-in-germany.com/en/working-in-germany/job-listings?tx_solr%5Bfilter%5D%5B2%5D=workingplan%3A1&tx_solr%5Bfilter%5D%5B13%5D=tstamp%3Aweek&tx_solr%5Bfilter%5D%5B15%5D=industry%3A7&tx_solr%5Bfilter%5D%5B16%5D=region%3A10">Make it in Germany</a> (the job listings: 174 training vacancies, roles and posting dates); <a href="https://www.make-it-in-germany.com/en/working-in-germany/job-listings?tx_solr%5Bfilter%5D%5B5%5D=tstamp%3Afortnight&tx_solr%5Bfilter%5D%5B9%5D=workingplan%3A1&tx_solr%5Bfilter%5D%5B13%5D=jobtype%3A1&tx_solr%5Bfilter%5D%5B14%5D=timelimit%3A1&tx_solr%5Bfilter%5D%5B15%5D=industry%3A7">Make it in Germany</a> (the salaried job listings: Requirement Manager, Electronics Technician and other November roles); <a href="https://www.make-it-in-germany.com/en/working-in-germany/job-listings?tx_solr%5Bfilter%5D%5B11%5D=jobtype%3A1&tx_solr%5Bfilter%5D%5B20%5D=tstamp%3Aweek&tx_solr%5Bfilter%5D%5B22%5D=timelimit%3A1&tx_solr%5Bfilter%5D%5B23%5D=industry%3A7">Make it in Germany</a> (the salaried job listings: Chef, Industrial Engineer and other 25 November roles).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>How many jobs are listed on Make it in Germany?</h3><p>174 training vacancies in the latest view. 49 salaried in one view, 68 in another.</p><h3>Do the listings give the salaries?</h3><p>No, the listings we checked don't contain any salary information so applicants should check the individual employer's listing.</p><h3>What jobs are in demand in Germany?</h3><p>Doctors, nurses, engineers, IT specialists, scientists, craft workers, transport workers and green jobs, according to Make it in Germany.</p><h3>Where do I apply?</h3><p>Through the Make it in Germany job listings, then follow the link to the employer's application page.</p>
$$,
$$<p>Germany's official 'Make it in Germany' job exchange is listing skilled and training vacancies throughout the country, with new vacancies added in late November 2026. Jobs in Germany in this roundup cover engineers, electricians, mechanics, cooks and chefs, and applications go in through the employer's own listing on the exchange.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>Make it in Germany job exchange, Federal Government of Germany; employers include BMW, Rolls-Royce Deutschland, Michelin, TU Bergakademie Freiberg and Dussmann Service</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Requirement-Manager, Electronics Technician, Engineer - Mechanical Engineering, Aircraft Mechanic, Chef, Cook, Industrial Engineer, Mechatronics Technician, Electrician</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Roles posted 1 to 25 November 2026; no closing dates stated on the listings checked</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through the Make it in Germany job listings, then to the employer's own application page</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Varies by role; recognised vocational qualification or engineering degree for the skilled posts</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Application to the employer; skilled-worker visa rules apply to applicants from outside the EU</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What jobs in Germany involve</h2><p>The latest salaried posts are a Requirement Manager (software engineering) in Nurnberg (23/25 Nov 2026), an Electronics Technician in operating technology with Wellpappe Alzenau (23 Nov 2026), and an Engineer in Mechanical Engineering with TU Bergakademie Freiberg (24 Nov 2026). A Chef post with Dussmann Service in Berlin and an Industrial Engineer post with Saarland University in Saarbrucken were both posted on 25 Nov 2026. Training posts include an Aircraft Mechanic apprenticeship with EXTRA Aircraft Maintenance in Hunxe, a two wheel mechatronics technician trainee with BMW in Bonn and a Process Mechanic with REHAU Industries in Velen (all 25 