<p> Maine is hiring in Augusta and across the state with vacancies in labour, health, transport and IT. Jobs in Maine USA in this roundup pay from $18.60 to $36.32 an hour, and the earliest closing date falls on 30 November 2026.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>State of Maine, various departments</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Employment and Training Specialist IV, Information System Support Specialist, Eligibility Specialist II, Highway Crew Supervisor, Customer Representative Associate II, Human Resources Assistant</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$18.60 to $36.32 an hour, or $59,987 to $84,718 a year for the specialist role</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Opened 13 to 24 November 2026; closing 30 November to 10 December 2026 depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through the State of Maine careers site on Workday</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Varies by role; Class C driving licence for the highway supervisor, with a Class A to be obtained in probation</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Online application and assessment; background checks, including fingerprinting, may be required</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What jobs in Maine USA involve</h2><p>The headline post is Employment and Training Specialist IV with the Department of Labor in Augusta, leading statewide implementation of the federal Rapid Reskill Dislocated Workers Grant, at $59,987.20 to $84,718.40 a year. The Department of Health and Human Services needs Eligibility Specialist II staff in Augusta to connect residents to MaineCare, food benefits, and cash assistance, at $22.51 to $31.50 an hour, with partial telework available. The Department of Transportation needs a Highway Crew Supervisor in Medway, overseeing a crew on highway, bridge and heavy equipment maintenance, at $25.71 to $36.32 an hour. The Office of Information Technology needs an Information System Support Specialist in Augusta to support endpoint security, vulnerability management, and software deployment, at $23.84 to $33.04 an hour. Readers looking more widely can browse <a href="https://growentix.cloud/usa">USA jobs</a> and our guide to <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/farm-worker-jobs-in-usa-on-h-2a-visa-pay-housing-and-how-to-apply-20261027">farm worker jobs in the USA on the H-2A visa</a>.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p> Employment and Training Specialist: a good fit for a collaborative, results-driven individual with experience in employment and training programmes. Eligibility Specialist: a good fit for someone who wants to be connecting Mainers to health and food benefits. Highway Crew Supervisor: requires a valid Class C licence, ability to obtain a Class A licence during the probationary period and a 30 hour OSHA safety course in construction. The listings make it very clear that these positions are not eligible for visa sponsorship or STEM OPT extensions and that an I-9 will be completed upon hire.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p>The Employment and Training Specialist IV pays $59,987.20 to $84,718.40 a year. The Highway Crew Supervisor pays $25.71 to $36.32 an hour, the Information System Support Specialist pays $23.84 to $33.04 an hour including a 15 percent recruitment and retention stipend, the Eligibility Specialist II pays $22.51 to $31.50 an hour, the Human Resources Assistant pays $20.97 to $28.85 an hour, and the Customer Representative Associate II in Motor Vehicles pays $18.60 to $26.77 an hour. State roles carry Maine state employee benefits, including health cover, retirement and paid leave.</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply online through the State of Maine careers site on Workday; current state employees apply through the internal process in PRISM. The Eligibility Specialist II closes on 30 November 2026, the Employment and Training Specialist IV closes on 3 December 2026, the Information System Support Specialist closes on 4 December 2026, and the Highway Crew Supervisor closes on 10 December 2026. Paper applications can be requested by emailing the recruiting address given on each listing.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The listings don't state how many posts are available for each role and give no interview dates or start dates. They do state that the roles are not eligible for visa sponsorship, but they don't say whether any other immigration route would be accepted. The Customer Representative Associate II closed on 25 November 2026 so you should check the live Workday site for the current equivalent openings.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> State of Maine applications are free and no state department will ever ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://maine.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/en-US/Executive/details/Employment---Training-Spec-IV_R26-04744">State of Maine</a> (the Employment and Training Specialist IV listing: salary, dates and sponsorship note); <a href="https://maine.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/en-US/Executive/job/Augusta-Maine/Info-System-Support-Specialist_R26-04708">State of Maine</a> (the Information System Support Specialist listing: salary, dates and duties); <a href="https://www.talent.com/view?id=586973059572772832">Talent.com</a> (the Eligibility Specialist II listing reproduced: salary, dates and duties).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What's the highest paid role in Maine according to this list?</h3><p>The Employment and Training Specialist IV, at $59,987.20 to $84,718.40 a year.</p><h3>When do those Maine roles close?</h3><p>From 30th November to 10th December 2026 (depending on the role).</p><h3>Is visa sponsorship available?</h3><p>No, the listings make it absolutely clear that these positions are not eligible for visa sponsorship or STEM OPT extensions.</p><h3>Where do I apply?</h3><p>Online via the State of Maine careers site on Workday.</p>
