$$<p>New York State government is hiring in New York City, with roles across health, law, parks, tax and human rights open to the general public. Jobs in New York USA in this roundup were posted between 16 and 20 November 2026, and the earliest closing dates fall on 30 November 2026.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>State of New York, various agencies</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Assistant Attorney General, Park Police Officer Trainee, Food Inspector 1, Investigator (Human Rights Specialist 1), Vocational Rehabilitation Counselor, Auditor (Tax), Licensed Psychologist, Principal Court Analyst</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Posted 16 to 20 November 2026; closing 30 November 2026 to 29 January 2027 depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through StateJobsNY</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Varies by role; law degree for the Attorney General post, professional licences for psychologist and nursing roles</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Application and assessment through the StateJobsNY system; many roles are listed under NY HELPS, which waives the civil service exam</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What jobs in New York USA involve</h2><p>The headline post is Assistant Attorney General in the New York City Litigation Bureau, closing 18 December 2026. Parks, Recreation and Historic Preservation is hiring Park Police Officer Trainees for the Long Island and Central regions, closing 29 January 2027, and a Park Supervisor for Denny Farrell Riverbank State Park. The Department of Agriculture and Markets needs a Food Inspector in Kings County, the Division of Human Rights needs an Investigator, and the State Education Department is hiring Vocational Rehabilitation Counselors in the Bronx and Jamaica, Queens. The Department of Taxation and Finance is hiring Auditors, and the Office of Mental Health is hiring Licensed Psychologists and Associate Psychologists. Readers looking more widely can browse <a href="https://growentix.cloud/usa">USA jobs</a> and our guide to <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/caregiver-jobs-in-usa-for-foreigners-visa-pay-and-how-to-apply-20261026">caregiver jobs in the USA for foreigners</a>, which covers a different route into American work.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p>These vacancies are listed as open to the general public on StateJobsNY, so anyone who meets the stated qualifications can apply. Many are marked NY HELPS, the state's hiring programme that lets agencies appoint qualified candidates without a civil service examination. The Attorney General role is for a qualified lawyer, the psychologist posts need the relevant professional licence, and the Park Police Officer Trainee role is an entry route into state law enforcement. The vacancy table does not state any nationality restriction, but applicants must be authorised to work in the United States.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p>The vacancy table checked does not state salary figures for these roles, so no pay is claimed here. New York State posts are graded, with roles in this roundup ranging from Grade 10 for a Licensed Practical Nurse to Grade 28 for a Network Systems Engineer; the full salary for each grade is listed on the individual vacancy page on StateJobsNY. State roles carry New York State employee benefits, including health cover, retirement and paid leave.</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply online via StateJobsNY, searching by vacancy title or item number. The closing dates vary sharply: the Food Inspector closes 30 November 2026; the Human Rights Investigator and Vocational Rehabilitation Counselor close 7 December 2026; the Assistant Attorney General closes 18 December 2026; and the Park Police Officer Trainee closes 29 January 2027. Be sure to check the individual vacancy page for the specific closing date and required documentation as these will vary from post to post.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The vacancy table doesn't state how many posts are available for each post, and provides no salary information, interview dates or start dates in the version we checked. It gives no indication as to whether visa sponsorship is available so international applicants should check the individual vacancy page or contact the hiring agency prior to applying.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> New York State applications are free, and no state agency will ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment, or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://statejobs.ny.gov/public/vacancyTable.cfm?searchResults=Yes&Keywords&title&JurisClassID&AgID&isnyhelp&minDate&maxDate&cat7=7&cat8=8&cat9=9&cat4=4&region3=3&region8=8&region9=9&employmentType=Full-Time&gradeCompareType=GT&grade&SalMin">StateJobsNY</a> (the general public vacancy list: positions, grades, dates posted and dates closed); <a href="https://statejobs.ny.gov/public/vacancyTable.cfm?searchResults=yes&minDate=11/19/26&maxDate=11/19/26">StateJobsNY</a> (the 19 November 2026 postings: Park Police Officer Trainee, Auditor and Psychologist roles).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>When do those New York roles close?</h3><p>From 30th November 2026 for the Food Inspector post to 29th January 2027 for the Park Police Officer Trainee posts (depending on the post).</p><h3>What is NY HELPS?</h3><p>It's the New York State hiring programme which allows agencies to appoint qualified candidates without a civil service examination.</p><h3>Are these posts open to the public?</h3><p>Yes the vacancies in this roundup are on the StateJobsNY general public page.</p><h3>Where do I apply?</h3><p>Online via StateJobsNY, searching by vacancy title or item number.</p>
$$,
