-- jobs-in-us-post-office-20261127 (usa; USA; verifiedAt 2026-11-27)
INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt", "verifiedAt", "authorName")
VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'jobs-in-us-post-office-20261127', 'usa', 'USA',
'Jobs in US Post Office: USPS Roles Pay $19 to $38 an Hour',
'Jobs in US Post Office: USPS Roles Pay $19 to $38 an Hour',
'Jobs in US Post Office roles are open nationwide, with USPS hiring carriers, clerks and maintenance staff at $19.02 to $38.29 an hour through usps.com/careers.',
'Jobs in US Post Office roles are open nationwide, with USPS hiring carriers, clerks and maintenance staff at $19.02 to $38.29 an hour through usps.com/careers.',
$$<p>The United States Postal Service is hiring across the country, from delivery and counter roles to maintenance and technical posts. Jobs in US Post Office openings in this roundup pay from $19.02 to $38.29 an hour, and applications go in online only through the USPS careers portal.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>United States Postal Service (USPS)</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>City Carrier Assistant, Rural Carrier Associate, Postal Support Employee, Mail Handler Assistant, Holiday Clerk Assistant, Electronic Technician, Automotive Technician, Maintenance Mechanic, Laborer Custodial</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$19.02 to $38.29 an hour, depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Postings are updated frequently; the Texas holiday and rural carrier window ran 6 to 10 November 2026 and the St Paul maintenance fair was 25 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online only at www.usps.com/careers</td></tr><tr><td>Age limit</td><td>Applicants must be 18, or 16 with a high school diploma</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>High school diploma or equivalent for entry roles; a valid state driving licence and safe driving record for rural carrier roles</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Online application, drug screening and a background investigation</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What jobs in US Post Office involve</h2><p>City Carrier Assistants deliver mail on city routes; Rural Carrier Associates serve rural and suburban households. They may also sell stamps and money orders, and Postal Support Employees and Mail Handler Assistants work in post offices and processing plants. Holiday Clerk Assistants staff retail counters during the Christmas peak, selling postal products and accepting mail and packages. Maintenance roles are more technical: Electronic Technicians, Automotive Technicians, Building Equipment Mechanics and Maintenance Mechanics keep vehicles, buildings and mail processing equipment running. Readers weighing other American employers can browse <a href="https://growentix.cloud/usa">USA jobs</a> and our guide to <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/amazon-warehouse-jobs-pay-shifts-roles-and-how-to-apply-20261031">Amazon warehouse jobs</a>, which also hires at scale for the holiday season.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p>Entry roles are open to applicants aged 18, or 16 with a high school diploma, who can pass drug screening and a background investigation. Rural carrier applicants need a valid state driving licence and must demonstrate and maintain a safe driving record. Maintenance posts suit hands-on problem solvers with technical or mechanical experience. The releases do not state any nationality restriction, but applicants must be eligible to work for a federal employer in the United States.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p>Entry pay is $19.02/hr for Mail Handler Assistants, $20.74 to $23.68 for Postal Support Employee clerks, $21.21 for City Carrier Assistants and $21.89 for Rural Carrier Associates. Holiday Clerk Assistants are paid $21.44/hr. Career city carriers start at $52,510 and can go up to $83,226, career clerks up to $79,802 to $81,053. Maintenance pay is higher with Laborer Custodial at $24.05/hr, Automotive Technician at $32.81, Maintenance Mechanic at $32.33, Lead Automotive Technician and Building Equipment Mechanic at $36.45 and Electronic Technician at $38.29. All career posts come with federal benefits (health and life insurance, retirement plan, savings plan with employer contribution, annual and sick leave and 11 paid federal holidays).</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply online only at www.usps.com/careers (postings are updated quite frequently so applicants should check back often). Job fairs are also held (e.g. the St Paul maintenance fair on 25 Nov 2026) which allow applicants to meet the hiring staff in person, however no interviews are held at the fairs and all applications are still submitted online. The Texas holiday clerk and rural carrier window ran from 6 to 10 November 2026, so readers should check the live portal for the current openings in your area.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The releases do not say how many posts are available in each location, and they give no interview dates or start dates. They do not state whether visa sponsorship is available, and the pay figures for rural carriers were published before a 2.5 percent raise effective 14 November 2026, so the live posting is the figure to trust. No closing date is given for most of the maintenance and entry roles, which are listed as open until filled.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> USPS applications are free and the Postal Service will never ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://about.usps.com/newsroom/local-releases/mn/2026/1116-united-states-postal-service-maintenance-career-fair-in-st-paul.htm">USPS</a> (St Paul maintenance career fair: positions, pay and date); <a href="https://about.usps.com/newsroom/local-releases/tx/2026/1105-usps-is-ready-to-welcome-new-team-members.htm">USPS</a> (Texas holiday clerk and rural carrier release: pay, locations and application period); <a href="https://www.empireresume.com/blog/working-for-usps/">Empire Resume</a> (2026 USPS pay scale: entry level and career level rates confirmed against union charts as of 24 November 2026).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>How much do the entry level USPS jobs pay?</h3><p>From $19.02 an hour for Mail Handler Assistants to $21.89 for Rural Carrier Associates, with clerks at $20.74 to $23.68.</p><h3>Where do I apply for USPS jobs?</h3><p>Apply online only at www.usps.com/careers; job fairs do not take applications or conduct interviews.</p><h3>What's the minimum age to apply?</h3><p>Applicants must be 18, or 16 with a high school diploma.</p><h3>Do USPS jobs come with benefits?</h3><p>Yes, career posts include health and life insurance, a retirement plan, a savings plan with employer contributions, annual and sick leave and 11 paid federal holidays.</p>
$$,
$$<p>The United States Postal Service is hiring across the country, from delivery and counter roles to maintenance and technical posts. Jobs in US Post Office openings in this roundup pay from $19.02 to $38.29 an hour, and applications go in online only through the USPS careers portal.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>United States Postal Service (USPS)</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>City Carrier Assistant, Rural Carrier Associate, Postal Support Employee, Mail Handler Assistant, Holiday Clerk Assistant, Electronic Technician, Automotive Technician, Maintenance Mechanic, Laborer Custodial</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$19.02 to $38.29 an hour, depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Postings are updated frequently; the Texas holiday and rural carrier window ran 6 to 10 November 2026 and the St Paul maintenance fair was 25 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online only at www.usps.com/careers</td></tr><tr><td>Age limit</td><td>Applicants must be 18, or 16 with a high school diploma</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>High school diploma or equivalent for entry roles; a valid state driving licence and safe driving record for rural carrier roles</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Online application, drug screening and a background investigation</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What jobs in US Post Office involve</h2><p>City Carrier Assistants deliver mail on city routes; Rural Carrier Associates serve rural and suburban households. They may also sell stamps and money orders, and Postal Support Employees and Mail Handler Assistants work in post offices and processing plants. Holiday Clerk Assistants staff retail counters during the Christmas peak, selling postal products and accepting mail and packages. Maintenance roles are more technical: Electronic Technicians, Automotive Technicians, Building Equipment Mechanics and Maintenance Mechanics keep vehicles, buildings and mail processing equipment running. Readers w