window ran from 6 to 10 November 2026, so readers should check the live portal for the current openings in your area.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The releases do not say how many posts are available in each location, and they give no interview dates or start dates. They do not state whether visa sponsorship is available, and the pay figures for rural carriers were published before a 2.5 percent raise effective 14 November 2026, so the live posting is the figure to trust. No closing date is given for most of the maintenance and entry roles, which are listed as open until filled.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> USPS applications are free and the Postal Service will never ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://about.usps.com/newsroom/local-releases/mn/2026/1116-united-states-postal-service-maintenance-career-fair-in-st-paul.htm">USPS</a> (St Paul maintenance career fair: positions, pay and date); <a href="https://about.usps.com/newsroom/local-releases/tx/2026/1105-usps-is-ready-to-welcome-new-team-members.htm">USPS</a> (Texas holiday clerk and rural carrier release: pay, locations and application period); <a href="https://www.empireresume.com/blog/working-for-usps/">Empire Resume</a> (2026 USPS pay scale: entry level and career level rates confirmed against union charts as of 24 November 2026).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>How much do the entry level USPS jobs pay?</h3><p>From $19.02 an hour for Mail Handler Assistants to $21.89 for Rural Carrier Associates, with clerks at $20.74 to $23.68.</p><h3>Where do I apply for USPS jobs?</h3><p>Apply online only at www.usps.com/careers; job fairs do not take applications or conduct interviews.</p><h3>What's the minimum age to apply?</h3><p>Applicants must be 18, or 16 with a high school diploma.</p><h3>Do USPS jobs come with benefits?</h3><p>Yes, career posts include health and life insurance, a retirement plan, a savings plan with employer contributions, annual and sick leave and 11 paid federal holidays.</p>
