INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt", "verifiedAt", "authorName")
VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'jobs-in-usa-los-angeles-20261127', 'usa', 'USA',
'Jobs in USA Los Angeles: City Roles Pay Up to $293,886',
'Jobs in USA Los Angeles: City Roles Pay Up to $293,886',
'Jobs in USA Los Angeles are open with the City of Los Angeles, with 120 full-time openings including a Port Pilot at $264,758 to $293,886 a year.',
'Jobs in USA Los Angeles are open with the City of Los Angeles, with 120 full-time openings including a Port Pilot at $264,758 to $293,886 a year.',
$$<p>The City of LA is hiring across the board with 120 full time positions listed on their personnel site. Jobs in USA Los Angeles in this roundup pay from $54,622 to $293,886 a year, and the earliest closing dates fall on 30 November 2026.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>City of Los Angeles</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Police Psychologist I, Director of Port Construction and Maintenance I, Database Architect, Delivery Driver I, Building Repairer, Evidence and Property Officer, Systems Analyst, Management Assistant</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$54,622 to $293,886 a year, depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Openings posted 17 to 20 November 2026; closing 30 November 2026 to 21 January 2027 depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through the City of Los Angeles personnel site and GovernmentJobs</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Varies by role; professional licences for psychologist, engineering and port roles</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Civil service application and assessment; some posts are transfer, exempt or emergency appointments</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What jobs in USA Los Angeles involve</h2><p>Headline post: Police Psychologist I with the Police Department ($138,497-$202,473, closes 21 Jan 2027). Harbor Department: Director of Port Construction and Maintenance I ($144,113.76-$210,679.20, closes 4 Dec 2026) and a Civil Engineering Drafting Technician. General Services: Delivery Driver I ($56,021.04-$69,593.04) and a Materials Testing Technician II. All departments have a Building Repairer opening ($57,858-$115,863) and a Database Architect ($127,973-$180,758). Police Department also have an Evidence and Property Officer. IT Agency and Harbor Department both have Systems Analysts. For the full list, have a look at <a href="https://growentix.cloud/usa">USA jobs</a> and our guide to <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/warehouse-jobs-in-usa-for-foreigners-visa-pay-and-how-to-apply-20261025">warehouse jobs in the USA for foreigners</a>.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p>Many of the openings are civil service posts open to the public. Some are transfer, exempt or emergency appointments which will have different eligibility rules so applicants should check the type of appointment on the individual listing. The Police Psychologist requires the relevant professional qualification, the Port and Engineering roles require professional licences and the Delivery Driver and Building Repairer roles are for experienced tradespeople. The listings do not state any nationality restriction, but applicants must be authorised to work in the US.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p>Pay varies significantly by role. Police Psychologist I pays $138,497 to $202,473 a year; the Director of Port Construction and Maintenance I is $144,113.76-$210,679.20; Database Architect pays $127,973 to $180,758; and the Financial Development Officer is $118,389-$185,727. Evidence and Property Officer is $67,776-$93,834; Management Assistant is $65,396.16-$95,588.64; Delivery Driver I pays $56,021.04 to $69,593.04; and the Administrative Clerk is $54,622-$71,639. The Port Pilot (which is $264,758-$293,886) closed on 19th November 2026. All City roles come with the City of Los Angeles benefits (health, retirement, paid leave etc).</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply online via the City of Los Angeles personnel site which directs civil service applicants. Closing dates vary: Systems Analysts close 30th November and 2nd December 2026; Delivery Driver, Building Repairer and Database Architect close 3rd December 2026; Director of Port Construction and Maintenance closes 4th December 2026 and Police Psychologist closes 21st January 2027. Applicants should check the individual posting to see what the job type, as transfer and promotional posts are not open to everyone.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The opening list gives no indication of how many posts there are for each role, no interview dates or start dates. It doesn't say whether visa sponsorship is available so international applicants should check directly with the City of Los Angeles prior to applying. Some of the listings are transfer/promotional posts which are not open to the general public.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> City of Los Angeles applications are free and no city department will ever ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://personnel.lacity.gov/jobs/index.cfm?sort=startdate&amt=25&shift=F&page=9">City of Los Angeles Personnel</a> (the openings list: roles, salaries and closing dates); <a href="https://personnel.lacity.gov/jobs/index.cfm?sort=enddate&amt=50&NUk6tn=VIGwiETA7H">City of Los Angeles Personnel</a> (the openings list sorted by closing date: Port Pilot, Director of Housing and other roles); <a href="https://personnel.lacity.gov/jobs/index.cfm?sort=datez&amt=100&NUk6tn=VIGwiETA7H&page=1">City of Los Angeles Personnel</a> (the openings list sorted by post date: Police Psychologist, Delivery Driver and other November roles).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>How many full-time jobs does the City of Los Angeles list?</h3><p>120 full time posts were listed on the personnel site in the version we checked.</p><h3>What's the best paid open role?</h3><p>The Police Psychologist I, $138,497 to $202,473 a year, closing 21 January 2027.</p><h3>When do the majority of these roles close?</h3><p>Between 30 November and 4 December 2026 for the roles in this round-up (with the Police Psychologist closing a bit later on 21st January 2027).</p><h3>Where do I apply?</h3><p>Via the City of Los Angeles personnel site which directs civil service applicants to GovernmentJobs.</p>
$$,
