-- remote-jobs-amazon-20261127 (remote; Remote; verifiedAt 2026-11-27)
INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt", "verifiedAt", "authorName")
VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'remote-jobs-amazon-20261127', 'remote', 'Remote',
'Remote Jobs Amazon: Support Roles Pay Up to $31.10 an Hour',
'Remote Jobs Amazon: Support Roles Pay Up to $31.10 an Hour',
'Remote jobs Amazon listings include a remote HR Contact Center role at $17.78 to $31.10 an hour and Selling Partner Support at $16.05 to $28.07 an hour.',
'Remote jobs Amazon listings include a remote HR Contact Center role at $17.78 to $31.10 an hour and Selling Partner Support at $16.05 to $28.07 an hour.',
$$<p>Amazon are hiring for remote customer facing roles in the US (support and HR contact centre roles). Remote jobs Amazon listings in this roundup pay from $16.05 to $31.10 an hour, and applications go in through Amazon's own jobs site.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>Amazon</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Remote HR Contact Center Professional, Selling Partner Support Specialist, Customer Service Associate</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$16.05 to $31.10 an hour, depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Listings live in November 2026; applications accepted on an ongoing basis</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through amazon.jobs</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>High school diploma or equivalent; six months of HR and customer service experience for the HR role, one year of customer support for Selling Partner Support</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Online application and assessment; training is provided</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What remote jobs Amazon involve</h2><p>The Remote HR Contact Centre Professional is a phone intensive role where you'll be answering HR questions from Amazon employees around the world via phone and chat, on a flexible schedule that can include evenings, weekends, and overnight hours. It is a seasonal role and there is the potential for extension or conversion to permanent depending on performance and business needs. The Selling Partner Support Specialist handles complex, high impact cases for Amazon's marketplace sellers, protecting the marketplace from fraud and abuse and resolving the issues that don't have an obvious answer. The Customer Service Associate role is to support customers with their orders and service issues via phone and email. If you're looking at remote options then you can browse the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/remote">remote jobs</a> and our guide to <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/remote-customer-service-jobs-no-experience-what-employers-actually-want-20261019">remote customer service jobs with no experience</a>.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p> HR Contact Centre: requires a high school diploma or equivalent, at least six months HR experience and six months customer service experience. Selling Partner Support Specialist: requires at least one year customer support/contact centre experience and experience working independently in a remote environment. Customer Service Associate: open to applicants with no experience. The Selling Partner Support role is available in most US states (excluding NY and CA). All three roles require a reliable home workspace and high speed internet.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p>The Remote HR Contact Center Professional is in the range of $17.78-$31.10/hr, the Selling Partner Support Specialist is $16.05-$28.07/hr and the Customer Service Associate role is advertised from $15 an hour, with an estimated range of $20.70 to $25.30 an hour on one job board, though that figure is an estimate rather than a posted rate. Amazon provides benefits from day one which include employee assistance, mental health support, a medical advice line, and 401(k) matching, with medical, dental and vision coverage for eligible roles.</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply online via amazon.jobs, searching for the role title. The HR Contact Centre listing went live on 7 November 2026 and was updated on 11 November. The Selling Partner Support listing went live on 20 November 2026. Applications are accepted on an ongoing basis and the listings can close very quickly once a sufficient pool of candidates has been received so it is advisable to apply as early as possible rather than waiting for a closing date.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The listings provide no closing date and no post count, and give no start date. The Customer Service Associate pay is listed as an estimate on a third party board rather than the actual Amazon rate so the live Amazon listing is the one to go by. None of the listings indicate whether visa sponsorship is available and the HR role is seasonal so permanent conversion is possible but not assured.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> The Amazon applications are free and Amazon will never ask you to pay anything in exchange for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://ratracerebellion.com/remote-hr-contact-center-professional-26/">Rat Race Rebellion</a> (the Amazon Remote HR Contact Centre listing: pay, hours and requirements); <a href="https://ratracerebellion.com/2026/11/20/">Rat Race Rebellion</a> (the Amazon Remote Selling Partner Support listing of 20 November 2026); <a href="https://www.glassdoor.com/Job/us-remote-customer-service-jobs-SRCH_IL.0,2_IN1_KO3,26.htm?fromAge=3&locId=1&locT=N&sortBy=date_desc">Glassdoor</a> (the Amazon Selling Partner Support listing as reproduced on Glassdoor: pay, location exclusions and benefits).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>How much do remote Amazon Support roles pay?</h3><p>From $16.05 to $31.10 an hour depending on the role.</p><h3>Do I need any experience for Amazon remote customer service?</h3><p>The Customer Service Associate role is listed as open to applicants with no experience. The HR and Selling Partner roles on the other hand require six months to a year of relevant experience.</p><h3>Where do I apply?</h3><p>Online via amazon.jobs searching for the role title.</p><h3>Are these roles available in every US state?</h3><p>No, the Selling Partner Support role excludes New York and California. Applicants should check the live listing for their state.</p>
$$,
$$<p>Amazon are hiring for remote customer facing roles in the US (support and HR contact centre roles). Remote jobs Amazon listings in this roundup pay from $16.05 to $31.10 an hour, and applications go in through Amazon's own jobs site.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>Amazon</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Remote HR Contact Center Professional, Selling Partner Support Specialist, Customer Service Associate</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$16.05 to $31.10 an hour, depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Listings live in November 2026; applications accepted on an ongoing basis</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through amazon.jobs</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>High school diploma or equivalent; six months of HR and customer service experience for the HR role, one year of customer support for Selling Partner Support</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Online application and assessment; training is provided</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What remote jobs Amazon involve</h2><p>The Remote HR Contact Centre Professional is a phone intensive role where you'll be answering HR questions from Amazon employees around the world via phone and chat, on a flexible schedule that can include evenings, weekends, and overnight hours. It is a seasonal role and there is the potential for extension or conversion to permanent depending on performance and business needs. The Selling Partner Support Specialist handles complex, high impact cases for Amazon's marketplace sellers, protecting the marketplace from fraud and abuse and resolving the issues that don't have an obvious answer. The Customer Service Associate role is to support customers with their orders and service issues via phone and email. If you're looking at remote options then you can browse the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/remote">remote jobs</a> and our guide to <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/remote-customer-service-jobs-no-experience-what-employers-actual