te whether visa sponsorship is available and the HR role is seasonal so permanent conversion is possible but not assured.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> The Amazon applications are free and Amazon will never ask you to pay anything in exchange for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://ratracerebellion.com/remote-hr-contact-center-professional-26/">Rat Race Rebellion</a> (the Amazon Remote HR Contact Centre listing: pay, hours and requirements); <a href="https://ratracerebellion.com/2026/11/20/">Rat Race Rebellion</a> (the Amazon Remote Selling Partner Support listing of 20 November 2026); <a href="https://www.glassdoor.com/Job/us-remote-customer-service-jobs-SRCH_IL.0,2_IN1_KO3,26.htm?fromAge=3&locId=1&locT=N&sortBy=date_desc">Glassdoor</a> (the Amazon Selling Partner Support listing as reproduced on Glassdoor: pay, location exclusions and benefits).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>How much do remote Amazon Support roles pay?</h3><p>From $16.05 to $31.10 an hour depending on the role.</p><h3>Do I need any experience for Amazon remote customer service?</h3><p>The Customer Service Associate role is listed as open to applicants with no experience. The HR and Selling Partner roles on the other hand require six months to a year of relevant experience.</p><h3>Where do I apply?</h3><p>Online via amazon.jobs searching for the role title.</p><h3>Are these roles available in every US state?</h3><p>No, the Selling Partner Support role excludes New York and California. Applicants should check the live listing for their state.</p>
$$,
ARRAY['https://ratracerebellion.com/remote-hr-contact-center-professional-26/', 'https://ratracerebellion.com/2026/11/20/', 'https://www.glassdoor.com/Job/us-remote-customer-service-jobs-SRCH_IL.0,2_IN1_KO3,26.htm?fromAge=3&locId=1&locT=N&sortBy=date_desc'], NOW(), NOW(), NOW(), '2026-11-27'::timestamptz, NULL) ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;

-- remote-jobs-customer-service-20261127 (remote; Remote; verifiedAt 2026-11-27)
INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt", "verifiedAt", "authorName")
VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'remote-jobs-customer-service-20261127', 'remote', 'Remote',
'Remote Jobs Customer Service: CVS and UnitedHealth Hiring',
'Remote Jobs Customer Service: CVS and UnitedHealth Hiring',
'Remote jobs customer service roles are open at CVS Health and UnitedHealth Group, paying $16 to $31.30 an hour for fully remote support work in the USA.',
'Remote jobs customer service roles are open at CVS Health and UnitedHealth Group, paying $16 to $31.30 an hour for fully remote support work in the USA.',
$$<p>Large American health employers are on the hunt for remote customer service staff with CVS Health and UnitedHealth Group both advertising fully remote roles. Remote jobs customer service posts in this roundup pay from $16 to $42.35 an hour, and applications go in through each employer's own careers site.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>CVS Health and UnitedHealth Group</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Customer Service Representative, Medicare Service Advocate, Benefits Verification Specialist, Senior Claim Benefit Specialist, Senior Customer Service Representative</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$16 to $42.35 an hour, depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Listings live in November 2026; CVS senior claims role published 24 November 2026; applications accepted on an ongoing basis</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through jobs.cvshealth.com and careers.unitedhealthgroup.com</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>One year of customer service experience for the Medicare Service Advocate; prior remote work experience for the CVS representative role</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Online application and assessment, followed by paid training</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What remote jobs customer service involve</h2><p> CVS Health Customer Service Representative takes inbound calls from providers, pharmacies and members and provides professional phone assistance via the criteria based prior authorisation process on a 40 hour schedule (mon-Sun 8 am- 9 pm ET) after 12 weeks of training. The Medicare Service Advocate works in the Medicare Stars Member Advocacy Center. The Benefits Verification Specialist verifies insurance coverage and prior authorisation details for specialty therapy patients. The Senior Claim Benefit Specialist reviews and adjudicates complex medical claims and also coaches colleagues on the more complex issues. At UnitedHealth Group the Customer Service Representative will assist the patient in routing their appointment and care requests, answer their questions, update their records and help to coordinate the next steps. If you're looking at remote options you can have a browse through our <a href="https://growentix.cloud/remote">remote jobs</a> and our <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/remote-data-entry-jobs-no-experience-where-beginners-can-actually-start-20261018">remote data entry jobs with no experience</a> guide.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p> CVS representative: requires prior remote work experience, a high speed internet connection (hardwired to the router), a quiet private remote work environment free from distraction, and the ability to provide your own transport for occasional on-site support within 50 miles of a CVS Caremark location. Medicare Service Advocate: requires one year of customer service experience in any line of business. UnitedHealth Group: remote but only for residents of Massachusetts (within commuting distance of Southborough where the training is done in person for 6-12 weeks). CVS Benefits Verification Specialist: must live within 60 minutes of Malvern, PA; Mendota Heights, MN or San Diego, CA.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p> CVS Customer Service Rep $17.00- $28.46/hr, Medicare Service Advocate pays $17 to $31.30, Senior Claim Benefit Specialist $18.50- $42.35. UnitedHealth Group Customer Service Representative pays $16 to $29 an hour, and a Senior Customer Service Rep at UnitedHealth Group is listed at $52,000 a year, or $18 to $32 an hour. CVS offers 401(k) match, dental, health and vision insurance, paid vacation and health & wellness programmes.</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply online through jobs.cvshealth.com for CVS roles, searching by requisition number, and through careers.unitedhealthgroup.com for UnitedHealth Group roles. The CVS Senior Claim Benefit Specialist was published on 24 November 2026 and has no application deadline, as CVS accepts applications on an ongoing basis. The CVS Benefits Verification Specialist application window closed on 22 November 2026, so readers should check the live CVS careers site for the current equivalent openings.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The listings give no post counts or start dates (the CVS representative listing gives no closing date). The location rules are very strict and vary by role so people outside of the stated areas should not assume they can apply. None of the listings indicate whether visa sponsorship is available so international applicants should check directly with the employer prior to applying.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> CVS Health and UnitedHealth Group applications are free and neither of those employers will ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://www.flexjobs.com/gjw/cvs_health/customer-service-representative/publicjobs?id=4151b8d0-3445-46e6-a324-33043e88a220">FlexJobs</a> (the CVS Health Customer Service Representative listing: pay, hours and training); <a href="https://jobs.cvshealth.com/us/en/job/R1052587/Senior-Claim-Benefit-Specialist-Remote?utm_source=Linkedin&utm_medium=phenom-feeds">CVS Health</a> (the Senior Claim Benefit Specialist listing: pay and ongoing applications); <a href="https://remotejobbrief.beehiiv.com/p/the-right-next-step-edition">Remote Job Brief</a> (the 18 November 2026 roundup: UnitedHealth Group and CVS roles, pay and location rules).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>How much do remote customer service jobs pay?</h3><p>From $16 to $42.35 an hour in this round up (depending on the role and the employer).</p><h3>Are these roles fully remote?</h3><p>The CVS roles are listed as 100% remote but some of them do require living near a specified office for training and/or occasional on-site support.</p><h3>Do I need remote work experience?</h3><p>Yes the CVS Customer Service Representative role does require prior remote work experience.</p><h3>Where do I apply?</h3><p>Via jobs.cvshealth.com for CVS roles and careers.unitedhealthgroup.com for UnitedHealth Group roles.</p>
$$,
$$<p>Large American health employers are on the hunt for remote customer service staff with CVS Health and UnitedHealth Group both advertising fully remote roles. Remote jobs customer service posts in this roundup pay from $16 to $42.35 an hour, and applications go in through each employer's own careers site.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>CVS Health and UnitedHealth Group</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Customer Service Representative, Medicare Service Advocate, Benefits Verification Specialist, Senior Claim Benefit Specialist, Senior Customer Service Representative</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$16 to $42.35 an hour, depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Listings live in November 2026; CVS senior claims role published 24 November 2026; applications accepted on an ongoing basis</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through jobs.cvshealth.com and careers.unitedhealthgroup.com</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>One year of customer service experience for the Medicare Service Advocate; prior remote work experience for the CVS representative role</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Online application and assessment, followed by paid training</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What remote jobs customer service involve</h2><p> CVS Health Customer Service Representative takes inbound calls from providers, pharmacies and members and provides professional phone assistance via the criteria based prior authorisation process on a 40 hour schedule (mon-Sun 8 am- 9 pm ET) after 12 weeks of training. The Medicare Service Advocate works in the Medicare Stars Member Advocacy Center. The Benefits Verification Specialist verifies insurance coverage and prior authorisation details for specialty therapy patients. The Senior Claim Benefit Specialist reviews and adjudicates complex medical claims and also coaches colleagues on the more complex issues. At UnitedHealth Group the Customer Service Representative will assist the patient in routing their appointment and care requests, answer their questions, update their records and help to coordinate the next steps. If you're looking at remote options you can have a browse through our <a href="https://growentix.cloud/remote">remote jobs</a> and our <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/remote-data-entry-jobs-no-experience-where-beginners-can-actually-start-20261018">remote data entry jobs with no experience</a> guide.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p> CVS representative: requires prior remote work experience, a high speed internet connection (hardwired to the router), a quiet private remote work environment free from distraction, and the ability to provide your own transport for occasional on-site support within 50 miles of a CVS Caremark location. Medicare Service Advocate: requires one year of customer service experience in any line of business. UnitedHealth Group: remote but only for residents of Massachusetts (within commuting distance of Southborough where the training is done in person for 6-12 weeks). CVS Benefits Verification Specialist: must live within 60 minutes of Malvern, PA; Mendota Heights, MN or San Diego, CA.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p> CVS Customer Service Rep $17.00- $28.46/hr, Medicare Service Advocate pays $17 to $31.30, Senior Claim Benefit Specialist $18.50- $42.35. UnitedHealth Group Customer Service Representative pays $16 to $29 an hour, and a Senior Customer Service Rep at UnitedHealth Group is listed at $52,000 a year, or $18 to $32 an hour. CVS offers 401(k) match, dental, health and vision insurance, paid vacation and health & wellness programmes.</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply online through jobs.cvshealth.com for CVS roles, searching by requisition number, and through careers.unitedhealthgroup.com for UnitedHealth Group roles. The CVS Senior Claim Benefit Specialist was published on 24 November 2026 and has no application deadline, as CVS accepts applications on an ongoing basis. The CVS Benefits Verification Specialist application window closed on 22 November 2026, so readers should check the live CVS careers site for the current equivalent openings.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The listings give no post counts or start dates (the CVS representative listing gives no closing date). The location rules are very strict and vary by role so people outside of the stated areas should not assume they can apply. None of the listings indicate whether visa sponsorship is available so international applicants should check directly with the employer prior to applying.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> CVS Health and UnitedHealth Group applications are free and neither of those employers will ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://www.flexjobs.com/gjw/cvs_health/customer-service-representative/publicjobs?id=4151b8d0-3445-46e6-a324-33043e88a220">FlexJobs</a> (the CVS Health Customer Service Representative listing: pay, hours and training); <a href="https://jobs.cvshealth.com/us/en/job/R1052587/Senior-Claim-Benefit-Specialist-Remote?utm_source=Linkedin&utm_medium=phenom-feeds">CVS Health</a> (the Senior Claim Benefit Specialist listing: pay and ongoing applications); <a href="https://remotejobbrief.beehiiv.com/p/the-right-next-step-edition">Remote Job Brief</a> (the 18 November 2026 roundup: UnitedHealth Group and CVS roles, pay and location rules).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>How much do remote customer service jobs pay?</h3><p>From $16 to $42.35 an hour in this round up (depending on the role and the employer).</p><h3>Are these roles fully remote?</h3><p>The CVS roles are listed as 100% remote but some of them do require living near a specified office for training and/or occasional on-site support.</p><h3>Do I need remote work experience?</h3><p>Yes the CVS Customer Service Representative role does require prior remote work experience.</p><h3>Where do I apply?</h3><p>Via jobs.cvshealth.com for CVS roles and careers.unitedhealthgroup.com for UnitedHealth Group roles.</p>
$$,
