(gen_random_uuid(), 'remote-jobs-data-entry-20261127', 'remote', 'Remote',
'Remote Jobs Data Entry: No Experience Roles Pay $10 to $25',
'Remote Jobs Data Entry: No Experience Roles Pay $10 to $25',
'Remote jobs data entry roles are open at DLN Consulting Group and APADCode, with no experience required, flexible hours and pay of $10 to $25 an hour.',
'Remote jobs data entry roles are open at DLN Consulting Group and APADCode, with no experience required, flexible hours and pay of $10 to $25 an hour.',
$$<p>Remote data entry is open to the absolute beginner with employers hiring typists and clerks who can work from home on flexible schedules. Remote jobs data entry posts in this roundup pay from $10 to $25 an hour, and none of them requires previous experience.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>DLN Consulting Group, APADCode, Wheel the World</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Remote Data Entry Specialist (Typist), Data Entry Specialist, Data Entry Clerk</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$10 to $25 an hour, depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Listings published 17 to 25 November 2026; no closing dates stated</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through Workable and Jobfound</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>High school diploma or equivalent; typing speed of 45 words per minute for the DLN role, 35 wpm for the Elite Job listing</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Online application and assessment; paid training is provided</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What remote jobs data entry involve</h2><p>The DLN Consulting Group Remote Data Entry Specialist accurately inputs, updates and maintains data in our internal systems and client databases on a flexible schedule. The APADCode Data Entry Specialist is a part time (10-20 hours per week) person who enters and checks data for a technology and business solutions company. The Wheel the World Data Entry Clerk is a fully remote worker who enters, updates, reviews and maintains accurate information in our company databases and internal systems. A further listing from Saisystems Health is a Data Support role (up to 20 hours per week) which involves cleaning and enriching customer records in a CRM with training provided in the first week. Anyone looking at remote options can have a look at the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/remote">remote jobs we have listed</a> and our guide to <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/virtual-assistant-jobs-for-beginners-skills-pay-where-to-start-20261019">virtual assistant jobs for beginners</a>.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p>These are all entry level roles and require no degree. The DLN role requires a high school diploma or equivalent and a minimum of 45wpm with high accuracy. The APADCode role requires only basic computer skills, good English communication and a willingness to learn. Previous data entry experience is a plus but not essential for either the DLN or Wheel the World roles. The APADCode role is very clear in stating that no technical background or any previous professional experience is required. Students, recent grads and career changers are all welcome.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p> APADCode role pays $10 to $25 an hour, depending on your qualifications and responsibilities. The DLN and Wheel the World listings give no salary figure in the versions checked, and a further beginner listing gives no fixed rate either, describing pay only as competitive and paid weekly. Data entry is generally paid by the hour and you should check the exact rate on the live listing prior to accepting an offer.</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply via the listing on Workable for the DLN role or via Jobfound for the APADCode and Wheel the World roles. The DLN listing was live on 19 November 2026, the Wheel the World listing on 17 November 2026 and the APADCode listing on 25 November 2026. None of the listings and they can close very quickly once they have a good pool of candidates so it's definitely worth applying early.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The listings provide no closing dates, no post counts and no start dates. Two of the three listings provide no salary figure so the pay range in this article is taken from the one listing that does. None of the listings state whether the roles are global or restricted to specific countries so applicants should check the live listing for location criteria before applying. Data entry is a role that attracts scams so applicants should be on the lookout for any listing that is asking for payment.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> Data entry applications are free and no real employer will ever ask you to pay anything for an application, for training or for a job.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://jobs.workable.com/view/5v67qo67nbg4753pn1x1WP/remote-data-entry-specialist-(typist)-in-new-york-at-dln-consulting-group">Workable</a> (the DLN Consulting Group Remote Data Entry Specialist listing: duties, typing speed and training); <a href="https://jobfound.org/job/apadcode-is-hiring-for-data-entry-specialist-india-remote-india-25-november-2026">Jobfound</a> (the APADCode Data Entry Specialist listing: pay, hours and no experience rule); <a href="https://jobfound.org/job/wheel-the-world-is-hiring-for-data-entry-clerk-remote-usa-17-november-2026">Jobfound</a> (the Wheel the World Data Entry Clerk listing: duties and entry level).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Do remote data entry jobs require experience?</h3><p>No, the roles in this roundup are very clear in that prior experience is preferred but not essential and there is paid training available.</p><h3>How much do they pay?</h3><p>From $10 to $25 an hour on the listing that states a rate; the other listings give no salary figure.</p><h3>What typing speed do I require?</h3><p>The DLN role requires 45 wpm with high accuracy.</p><h3>Are these roles full-time?</h3><p>Both the full time and part time options are listed, with the APADCode role at 10-20 hours per week.</p>
$$,
