ting that is asking for payment.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> Data entry applications are free and no real employer will ever ask you to pay anything for an application, for training or for a job.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://jobs.workable.com/view/5v67qo67nbg4753pn1x1WP/remote-data-entry-specialist-(typist)-in-new-york-at-dln-consulting-group">Workable</a> (the DLN Consulting Group Remote Data Entry Specialist listing: duties, typing speed and training); <a href="https://jobfound.org/job/apadcode-is-hiring-for-data-entry-specialist-india-remote-india-25-november-2026">Jobfound</a> (the APADCode Data Entry Specialist listing: pay, hours and no experience rule); <a href="https://jobfound.org/job/wheel-the-world-is-hiring-for-data-entry-clerk-remote-usa-17-november-2026">Jobfound</a> (the Wheel the World Data Entry Clerk listing: duties and entry level).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Do remote data entry jobs require experience?</h3><p>No, the roles in this roundup are very clear in that prior experience is preferred but not essential and there is paid training available.</p><h3>How much do they pay?</h3><p>From $10 to $25 an hour on the listing that states a rate; the other listings give no salary figure.</p><h3>What typing speed do I require?</h3><p>The DLN role requires 45 wpm with high accuracy.</p><h3>Are these roles full-time?</h3><p>Both the full time and part time options are listed, with the APADCode role at 10-20 hours per week.</p>
