(gen_random_uuid(), 'uk-civil-service-jobs-20261127', 'uk', 'UK',
'UK Civil Service Jobs: Roles Pay £24,645 to £93,308',
'UK Civil Service Jobs: Roles Pay £24,645 to £93,308',
'UK Civil Service jobs are open on Civil Service Jobs, with Companies House roles at £60,287 to £93,308 closing 29 November 2026 and 1,257 vacancies listed.',
'UK Civil Service jobs are open on Civil Service Jobs, with Companies House roles at £60,287 to £93,308 closing 29 November 2026 and 1,257 vacancies listed.',
$$<p>The UK Civil Service is recruiting across the departments with 1,257 posts listed on the Civil Service Jobs site. The UK Civil Service jobs in this round are ranging from £24,645 to £93,308 per annum and a number of the headline roles are closing on 29th November 2026.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>UK Civil Service: Companies House, Fair Work Agency, HM Prison and Probation Service, Ministry of Defence</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Deputy Community Interest Companies Regulator, Head of Technical Architecture, Evaluation Lead, Peer Mentor Co-ordinator, Case Administrator, Information Support Assistant</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>£24,645 to £93,308 a year, depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Companies House roles close 29 November 2026 at 23:55; many other roles closed 25 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through Civil Service Jobs</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Varies by role; senior technical and regulatory experience for the Companies House posts</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Application, sifting and interview under the Civil Service Success Profiles framework; selection on merit through a fair and open competition</td></tr><tr><td>Interview</td><td>Deputy Regulator interviews 14 and 15 December 2026 on Microsoft Teams; Head of Technical Architecture interviews week commencing 7 December 2026</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What UK Civil Service jobs involve</h2><p> Deputy Community Interest Companies Regulator at Companies House in Edinburgh (salary: £60,287- £66,765) plus a Civil Service defined benefit pension contribution of £17,465 on top of the starting salary. The Head of Technical Architecture at Companies House (salary: £76,312- £93,308) plus a digital, data and technology allowance of £4,350 to £11,000. Other open roles: Evaluation Lead with the Fair Work Agency (£42,391- £46,465), Peer Mentor Co-ordinator with HM Prison and Probation Service (£28,064- £33,549), Case Administrator (£24,645- £26,723), Information Support Assistant with the Mod (£27,866). For those looking more widely around the UK, you can browse <a href="https://growentix.cloud/uk">UK jobs</a> and our guide to <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/uk-nhs-jobs-visa-sponsorship-november-2026-20261121">UK NHS jobs with visa sponsorship</a>.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p>Civil Service Jobs vacancies are open to applicants who meet the Civil Service nationality and right-to-work requirements, and selection is on merit through fair and open competition. The Companies House senior roles need substantial regulatory or technical architecture experience, while the Case Administrator and Peer Mentor Co-ordinator roles are more accessible entry routes. Applications are submitted only through Civil Service Jobs, and communications come by email, so applicants should check their Civil Service Jobs account and spam folder regularly.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p>The Head of Technical Architecture pays £76,312 to £93,308 a year, and the Deputy Community Interest Companies Regulator pays £60,287 to £66,765. The Evaluation Lead pays £42,391 to £46,465, the Peer Mentor Co-ordinator pays £28,064 to £33,549, the Information Support Assistant pays £27,866, and the Case Administrator pays £24,645 to £26,723. Civil Service roles carry a defined benefit pension with an employer contribution of 28.97 percent on many posts, plus annual leave and flexible working.</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply online via Civil Service Jobs, searching by role title or reference number. The Companies House roles close on Sunday 29 November 2026 at 23.55 with sifting from 30 November 2026. The Deputy Regulator interviews are on 14 and 15 December 2026 on Microsoft Teams and the Head of Technical Architecture interviews are in the week commencing 7 December 2026. A number of the other roles in the 1,257 result search have already closed (on 25 November 2026) so it's worth filtering by closing date on the live site.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The listings don't state how many posts there are for each role and give no start dates. The Companies House adverts don't state whether visa sponsorship is available and applicants will have to meet the Civil Service nationality rules so international applicants should check the individual advert before applying. The closing dates are indicative only and may change.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> UK Civil Service applications are free and no department will ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://www.civilservicejobs.service.gov.uk/csr/index.cgi?SID=b3duZXI9NTA3MDAwMCZjb250ZXh0aWQ9MjIyNjUxOTA0JnNvcnQ9Y2xvc2luZyZwYWdlYWN0aW9uPXNlYXJjaGNvbnRleHQmcGFnZWNsYXNzPVNlYXJjaCZwYWdlPTImb3duZXJ0eXBlPWZhaXImcmVxc2lnPTE3OTU2NDc1MjItYjI3NmI0YzJhNWI3YWFhYTMzNDAwZWMwOTJlMzE2OWY2M2ViYTFhMQ%3D%3D&utm_content=6">Civil Service Jobs</a> (1,257 vacancies, salaries and closing dates); <a href="https://www.glassdoor.co.uk/job-listing/deputy-community-interest-companies-cic-regulator-companies-house-JV_IC3312271_KO0,49_KE50,65.htm?jl=1010323690492">Glassdoor</a> (the Companies House Deputy Regulator advert as reproduced there: salary, closing date and interview dates); <a href="https://www.glassdoor.co.uk/job-listing/head-of-technical-architecture-companies-house-JV_IC3312271_KO0,30_KE31,46.htm?jl=1010325716926">Glassdoor</a> (the Companies House Head of Technical Architecture advert as reproduced there: salary, allowance and dates).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>How many UK Civil Service vacancies are listed?</h3><p>1,257 results were listed on Civil Service Jobs in the version that we checked.</p><h3>When do the Companies House roles close?</h3><p>On Sunday 29th November 2026 at 23:55.</p><h3>What is the best-paid role in this roundup?</h3><p>The Head of Technical Architecture, at £76,312 to £93,308 a year.</p><h3>Where do I apply?</h3><p>Online only through Civil Service Jobs.</p>
$$,
$$<p>The UK Civil Service is recruiting across the departments with 1,257 posts listed on the Civil Service Jobs site. The UK Civil Service jobs in this round are ranging from £24,645 to £93,308 per annum and a number of the headline roles are closing on 29th November 2026.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>UK Civil Service: Companies House, Fair Work Agency, HM Prison and Probation Service, Ministry of Defence</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Deputy Community Interest Companies Regulator, Head of Technical Architecture, Evaluation Lead, Peer Mentor Co-ordinator, Case Administrator, Information Support Assistant</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>£24,645 to £93,308 a year, depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Companies House roles close 29 November 2026 at 23:55; many other roles closed 25 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through Civil Service Jobs</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Varies by role; senior technical and regulatory experience for the Companies House posts</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Application, sifting and interview under the Civil Service Success Profiles framework; selection on merit through a fair and open competition</td></tr><tr><td>Interview</td><td>Deputy Regulator interviews 14 and 15 December 2026 on Microsoft Teams; Head of Technical Architecture interviews week commencing 7 December 2026</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What UK Civil Service jobs involve</h2><p> Deputy Community Interest Companies Regulator at Companies House in Edinburgh (salary: £60,287- £66,765) plus a Civil Service defined benefit pension contribution of £17,465 on top of the starting salary. The Head of Technical Architecture at Companies House (salary: £76,312- £93,308) plus a digital, data and technology allowance of £4,350 to £11,000. Other open roles: Evaluation Lead with the Fair Work Agency (£42,391- £46,465), Peer Mentor Co-ordinator with HM Prison and Probation Service (£28,064- £33,549), Case Administrator (£24,645- £26,723), Information Support Assistant with the Mod (£27,866). For those looking more widely around the UK, you can browse <a href="https://growentix.cloud/uk">UK jobs</a> and our guide to <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/uk-nhs-jobs-visa-sponsorship-november-2026-20261121">UK NHS jobs with visa sponsorship</a>.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p>Civil Service Jobs vacancies are open to applicants who meet the Civil Service nationality and right-to-work requirements, and selection is on merit through fair and open competition. The Companies House senior roles need substantial regulatory or technical architecture experience, while the Case Administrator and Peer Mentor Co-ordinator roles are more accessible entry routes. Applications are submitted only through Civil Service Jobs, and communications come by email, so applicants should check their Civil Service Jobs account and spam folder regularly.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p>The Head of Technical Architecture pays £76,312 to £93,308 a year, and the Deputy Community Interest Companies Regulator pays £60,287 to £66,765. The Evaluation Lead pays £42,391 to £46,465, the Peer Mentor Co-ordinator pays £28,064 to £33,549, the Information Support Assistant pays £27,866, and the Case Administrator pays £24,645 to £26,723. Civil Service roles carry a defined benefit pension with an employer contribution of 28.97 percent on many posts, plus annual leave and flexible working.</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply online via Civil Service Jobs, searching by role title or reference number. The Companies House roles close on Sunday 29 November 2026 at 23.55 with sifting from 30 November 2026. The Deputy Regulator interviews are on 14 and 15 December 2026 on Microsoft Teams and the Head of Technical Architecture interviews are in the week commencing 7 December 2026. A number of the other roles in the 1,257 result search have already closed (on 25 November 2026) so it's worth filtering by closing date on the live site.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The listings don't state how many posts there are for each role and give no start dates. The Companies House adverts don't state whether visa sponsorship is available and applicants will have to meet the Civil Service nationality rules so international applicants should check the individual advert before applying. The closing dates are indicative only and may change.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> UK Civil Service applications are free and no department will ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://www.civilservicejobs.service.gov.uk/csr/index.cgi?SID=b3duZXI9NTA3MDAwMCZjb250ZXh0aWQ9MjIyNjUxOTA0JnNvcnQ9Y2xvc2luZyZwYWdlYWN0aW9uPXNlYXJjaGNvbnRleHQmcGFnZWNsYXNzPVNlYXJjaCZwYWdlPTImb3duZXJ0eXBlPWZhaXImcmVxc2lnPTE3OTU2NDc1MjItYjI3NmI0YzJhNWI3YWFhYTMzNDAwZWMwOTJlMzE2OWY2M2ViYTFhMQ%3D%3D&utm_content=6">Civil Service Jobs</a> (1,257 vacancies, salaries and closing dates); <a href="https://www.glassdoor.co.uk/job-listing/deputy-community-interest-companies-cic-regulator-companies-house-JV_IC3312271_KO0,49_KE50,65.htm?jl=1010323690492">Glassdoor</a> (the Companies House Deputy Regulator advert as reproduced there: salary, closing date and interview dates); <a href="https://www.glassdoor.co.uk/job-listing/head-of-technical-architecture-companies-house-JV_IC3312271_KO0,30_KE31,46.htm?jl=1010325716926">Glassdoor</a> (the Companies House Head of Technical Architecture advert as reproduced there: salary, allowance and dates).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>How many UK Civil Service vacancies are listed?</h3><p>1,257 results were listed on Civil Service Jobs in the version that we checked.</p><h3>When do the Companies House roles close?</h3><p>On Sunday 29th November 2026 at 23:55.</p><h3>What is the best-paid role in this roundup?</h3><p>The Head of Technical Architecture, at £76,312 to £93,308 a year.</p><h3>Where do I apply?</h3><p>Online only through Civil Service Jobs.</p>
