(gen_random_uuid(), 'aaron-rodgers-released-steelers-free-agent-20261127', 'news', 'USA',
'Aaron Rodgers released by Steelers, now a free agent',
'Aaron Rodgers released by Steelers, now a free agent',
'Aaron Rodgers released by the Pittsburgh Steelers on 25 November and went unclaimed on waivers, leaving the 42-year-old quarterback a free agent.',
'Aaron Rodgers released by the Pittsburgh Steelers on 25 November and went unclaimed on waivers, leaving the 42-year-old quarterback a free agent.',
$$<p>Aaron Rodgers released by the Pittsburgh Steelers on Wednesday 25 November, and went unclaimed on waivers the next day, leaving the four-time NFL most valuable player a free agent in what he has said is his final season.</p>

<table>
<tr><td>Player</td><td>Aaron Rodgers, quarterback, aged 42</td></tr>
<tr><td>Team</td><td>Pittsburgh Steelers</td></tr>
<tr><td>Benched</td><td>Tuesday night, 24 November 2026</td></tr>
<tr><td>Released</td><td>Wednesday 25 November 2026</td></tr>
<tr><td>Waivers</td><td>Cleared unclaimed, Thursday 26 November</td></tr>
<tr><td>Replacement</td><td>Mason Rudolph starts Friday 27 November vs Denver Broncos</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>What happened</h2>

<p>The Steelers announced late on Tuesday night that Rodgers would be inactive for Friday's game against the Denver Broncos, with Mason Rudolph taking over as starting quarterback, <a href="https://www.si.com/nfl/steelers/onsi/pittsburgh-steelers-bench-aaron-rodgers-mason-rudolph-starting-quarterback">Sports Illustrated</a> reported. Head coach Mike McCarthy said the benching was a coach's decision, made after the offence managed a combined 477 yards over its last two games and Pittsburgh lost two straight, failing to reach 20 points in either game.</p>

<p>Hours later Rodgers was on Wednesday's episode of The Pat McAfee Show criticising McCarthy, claiming he'd dozed off in team meetings, according to <a href="https://www.usatoday.com/story/sports/nfl/steelers/2026/11/25/aaron-rodgers-released-steelers/92962338007/">USA Today</a>. Rodgers said he'd not be coming back to the team having been benched and that he found out from teammate Pat Freiermuth rather than McCarthy. Less than two hours after that appearance the Steelers posted: "We have released QB Aaron Rodgers."</p>

<p>Rodgers was subject to waivers as his release came after the 10 November trade deadline and he went unclaimed on Thursday 26 November, making him an unrestricted free agent (per <a href="https://www.usatoday.com/story/sports/nfl/2026/11/26/aaron-rodgers-unclaimed-waivers-pittsburgh-steelers/92965763007/">USA Today</a> reported. Rodgers, who turns 43 on 2 December) was in his second season with Pittsburgh and his 22nd in the NFL, having previously stated that the 2026 season would be his final. His last game for the Steelers could therefore have been Sunday's 19-16 defeat to the Philadelphia Eagles.</p>

<h2>What the Aaron Rodgers released story means</h2>

<p>The release ends one of the most abrupt collapses of a star quarterback's career, from starter to unemployed in about 48 hours, and it leaves the Steelers to finish the season with Rudolph, who has been called on before to spark the offence. Pittsburgh, at 6-4, still has a winning record, but the public break with McCarthy, and the reports that the situation had been brewing for a while and reached the point of no return on Tuesday night, suggest the split was about trust as much as results.</p>

<p>For Rodgers the question is whether any team will go and sign a 42 year old QB who's just been released mid-season after publicly going on about his coach. Most of the teams have sorted their QBS by the trade deadline and former teammate Clay Matthews was one of those doubting another team would want him. If no team calls then his career will end not with a farewell game but with a benching, a TV appearance and a one line release. More sport in our <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/inter-miami-columbus-crew-playoff-upset-20261122">Inter Miami playoff upset</a> report and the wider world news is in our <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles">News</a> section.</p>

<h2>What the sources do not say</h2>

<p>None of the sources say whether Rodgers wants to play for another team, or whether any team has contacted him since he cleared waivers. The sources do not confirm McCarthy's response to the claim that he fell asleep in meetings, beyond reports that he has the full support of the Steelers organisation. It is also not stated whether Rodgers will make a formal retirement announcement, or when.</p>

<p>Sources: <a href="https://www.usatoday.com/story/sports/nfl/steelers/2026/11/25/aaron-rodgers-released-steelers/92962338007/">USA Today</a> for the release and the McAfee Show appearance; <a href="https://www.usatoday.com/story/sports/nfl/2026/11/26/aaron-rodgers-unclaimed-waivers-pittsburgh-steelers/92965763007/">USA Today</a> for the waivers outcome; <a href="https://www.si.com/nfl/steelers/onsi/pittsburgh-steelers-bench-aaron-rodgers-mason-rudolph-starting-quarterback">Sports Illustrated</a> for the benching and the Rudolph start; <a href="https://fieldlevelmedia.com/news/report-aaron-rodgers-steps-away-to-process-benching/">Field Level Media</a> for the Steelers' release post and the waiver deadline.</p>

<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>

<h3>Why was Aaron Rodgers released by the Steelers?</h3>
<p>He was benched on Tuesday 24th November following two poor offensive games and then went on to criticise head coach Mike McCarthy on The Pat McAfee Show on Wednesday, and said he would not return. The Steelers released him hours later.</p>

<h3>Is Aaron Rodgers a free agent now?</h3>
<p>Yes, he went unclaimed on waivers on Thursday 26th November and is now an unrestricted free agent. He's free to sign with any team.</p>

<h3>Who's the Steelers QB now?</h3>
<p>Mason Rudolph (who starts against the Broncos on Friday 27th November) with Will Howard on the bench.</p>
