-- bitcoin-price-holds-60000-november-slump-20261127 (news; Global; verifiedAt NULL)
INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt", "verifiedAt", "authorName")
VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'bitcoin-price-holds-60000-november-slump-20261127', 'news', 'Global',
'Bitcoin price holds $60,000 after November slump',
'Bitcoin price holds $60,000 after November slump',
'Bitcoin price held near $60,500 on 26 November after falling about 22% in the month, as a death cross formed and $7bn of options headed for expiry.',
'Bitcoin price held near $60,500 on 26 November after falling about 22% in the month, as a death cross formed and $7bn of options headed for expiry.',
$$<p>Bitcoin price was holding at around $60,500 on Thursday 26th November, having bounced back from an intraday low of around $57,500 the day before. It's been a very bad month for the coin in November having lost around 22% of its price this month.</p>

<table>
<tr><td>Asset</td><td>Bitcoin (BTC)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Price, 26 November</td><td>Around $60,500</td></tr>
<tr><td>Low, 25 November</td><td>About $57,500</td></tr>
<tr><td>November change</td><td>Down about 22% from about $77,500 on 1 November</td></tr>
<tr><td>Thanksgiving 2025</td><td>About $91,300, so down about 33.5% year on year</td></tr>
<tr><td>Market value</td><td>About $1.22 trillion</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>What happened</h2>

<p>Bitcoin was at around $60,560 on 26 November, up 1.39% in the 24 hours and down 3.67% over the seven days, according to Decrypt, as reported by <a href="https://bitcoininfonews.com/bitcoin-us-session-roundup-2026-11-26">BitcoinInfoNews</a>. The key technical development of the session was the formation of a death cross (the 50-day EMA at $71,478 crossing below the 200-day EMA at $74,516, both in a downward trend). The price had bounced back about 5% from its Wednesday low of $57,500 into the session and then hit a new intraday low of $55,100 on 21 November (a new bear market low).</p>

<p>Galaxy Research has retracted its 26 October call that the bear market in Bitcoin had ended in June 2026, following Bitcoin closing below its 50 week MA in the week ending 8 November and then falling below its 200 week MA at around $68,159 (same report). Wallets with between 10 and 10,000 BTC have shed some 150,000 coins since 2 November, <a href="https://coinedition.com/bitcoin-price-rebounds-as-santiment-flags-150k-btc-whale-drop/">CoinEdition</a> reported, citing Santiment data. US spot Bitcoin ETFS have now recorded a net outflow of $5.39 bn this month to 25 November, which is a record monthly outflow, according to <a href="https://financefeeds.com/bitcoin-price-november-month-end/">FinanceFeeds</a>.</p>

<p>Bitcoin was at just $60,700 on 26 November, compared with $91,324 it was at on Thanksgiving last year, a decline of 33.5 per cent, according to <a href="https://www.fvbb.com/ns/bitcoin-price-prediction-2027-btc-usd-today/332908">24/7 Wall St via FVBB</a>. The decline accelerated in late October, dropping from $80,801 on 27 October to $58,818 by 20 November.</p>

<h2>What the Bitcoin price means</h2>

<p>The death cross and Galaxy's reversal matter because they are the signals professional traders watch to judge whether a sell-off is a dip or a longer bear market, and both now point the wrong way for holders. Galaxy flagged a daily close below $58,525, the 30 June closing low, as a sign of a lower low, warning that a weekly close below that level has historically implied further falls of about 17 per cent towards $48,500, or a median fall of about 52 per cent towards $28,200 in past bear cycles. Against that, institutional buyers including Strive and Tudor Investment continued buying, and about $7 billion in Bitcoin options expire on Friday 28 November, which can sharpen price moves in either direction.</p>

<p>For ordinary holders, the numbers are stark: to finish November flat, Bitcoin would need to climb about 27.7 per cent back to $77,521 in four days, which FinanceFeeds describes as the month-end test. The market has now been in a bear market for 412 days, according to Galaxy. Our earlier report on the slide is <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/bitcoin-price-below-60000-20261125">Bitcoin price below $60,000</a>, and the latest from the wider world is in our <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles">News</a> section.</p>

<h2>What the sources do not say</h2>

<p>None of the sources say whether Bitcoin will hold above $58,525 into the month-end close, or what Friday's $7 billion options expiry will do to the price. The sources do not agree on a single cause for the sell-off, citing tariff threats, geopolitical tension, ETF outflows and technical selling in different measures. It is also not stated whether the whale selling since 2 November has finished or is continuing.</p>

<p>Sources: <a href="https://bitcoininfonews.com/bitcoin-us-session-roundup-2026-11-26">BitcoinInfoNews</a>, reporting Decrypt, for the price, the death cross and Galaxy's reversal; <a href="https://financefeeds.com/bitcoin-price-november-month-end/">FinanceFeeds</a> for the November fall, the ETF outflows and the month-end test; <a href="https://coinedition.com/bitcoin-price-rebounds-as-santiment-flags-150k-btc-whale-drop/">CoinEdition</a> for the whale selling; <a href="https://www.fvbb.com/ns/bitcoin-price-prediction-2027-btc-usd-today/332908">FVBB</a> for the Thanksgiving year-on-year comparison.</p>

<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>

<h3>What is the Bitcoin price today?</h3>
<p>Bitcoin was at around $60,500 on Thursday 26th November 2026 having bounced back from approximately $57,500 the day prior. Of course the price is always in flux so a live quote is advisable before you go on any figures.</p>

<h3>What is a Bitcoin death cross?</h3>
<p>It's when Bitcoin's 50-day MA drops below its 200-day MA. On 26 November the 50-day was at $71,478 and the 200-day was at $74,516 which was interpreted as a bearish signal.</p>

<h3>How much has Bitcoin dropped in November 2026?</h3>
<p>Approx 22% from around $77,500 on 1st November to around $60,500 on 26th November. The US spot Bitcoin ETFs had record $5.39 billion in outflows that month.</p>
