<p>Macy's, New York City and NBC made the decision on Wednesday, after the National Weather Service forecast strong to damaging winds and moderate to heavy rain across the region on Thanksgiving Day, <a href="https://www.cnn.com/2026/11/25/us/macys-thanksgiving-day-parade-postponed?cid=external-feeds_iluminar_meta">CNN</a> reported. The parade will now begin at 8.30 am ET on Saturday. The giant character balloons, which had already been inflated on Wednesday, were deflated and taken back to New Jersey to be prepared again for Saturday, a process normally spread over weeks compressed into about a day.</p>

<p>The storm was very severe across the eastern US. By Thursday evening over 900,000 homes and businesses were without power (mostly on the East Coast) and over 2,200 flights to and from US destinations were delayed with over 400 cancelled, according to the Associated Press via <a href="https://www.wvlt.tv/2026/11/26/severe-weather-across-us-expected-complicate-thanksgiving-travel/">WVLT</a>. New Jersey was under a state of emergency as were parts of New York. The Thanksgiving Day parade in Philadelphia was cancelled by the organisers (it was to be the oldest in the country) after they would ground the balloons.</p>

<p>New York City's safety rules prohibit the giant balloons from flying when sustained winds exceed 23 mph, or gusts exceed 34 mph, and Thursday morning gusts were forecast at roughly 35 to 40 mph, <a href="https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/2026/11/24/macys-parade-canceled-balloons-wind-noreaster/92938791007/">NorthJersey.com</a> reported. NBC instead broadcast a replay of the 2025 parade on Thursday morning, followed by the National Dog Show at noon ET.</p>

<h2>What the Macy's Thanksgiving Parade move means</h2>

<p>The parade itself will still be the 100th edition of an event which began in 1924 and organisers say it will be the largest it has ever been. It was cancelled three times during the Second World War (1942-1944) but has never previously been postponed before, according to <a href="https://www.aljazeera.com/amp/news/2026/11/26/storms-push-macys-thanksgiving-day-parade-in-new-york-city-to-saturday">Al Jazeera</a>. Macy's executive producer Will Coss stated that the safety of the participants and the spectators was always the number one thing and that they were hopeful that they would be able to put on the most spectacular parade in its history on Saturday.</p>

<p>Saturday looks much better with clear skies, 10 to 15 mph sustained winds and gusts around 20 mph (well within balloon limits). NBC will be broadcasting the rescheduled parade from 8.30 am in the Eastern, Central and Mountain time zones and at 7.30 am Pacific, and it will also stream on Peacock and on Telemundo. Mayor Zohran Mamdani (who will be missing the parade because of scheduled for the day) has stated there are no known specific or credible threats to the event. Travel advice for the holiday weekend is in our <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/thanksgiving-travel-2026-aaa-20261125">Thanksgiving travel 2026</a> guide and the wider world update is in our <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles">News</a> section.</p>

<h2>What the sources do not say</h2>

<p>The sources don't confirm that every band and marching group that travelled for Thursday will actually be able to participate on Saturday and Macy's has said they're still working through the logistics. They give no indication as to whether Saturday's weather will be as forecasted and the parade could still be impacted if the winds pick up and exceed the balloon limits. They also don't state how many spectators are expected on Saturday as opposed to a normal Thanksgiving Day crowd.</p>

<p>Sources: <a href="https://www.cnn.com/2026/11/25/us/macys-thanksgiving-day-parade-postponed?cid=external-feeds_iluminar_meta">CNN</a> for the postponement, the Saturday start time and the balloon deflation; <a href="https://www.aljazeera.com/amp/news/2026/11/26/storms-push-macys-thanksgiving-day-parade-in-new-york-city-to-saturday">Al Jazeera</a> for the 100th edition, the wartime cancellations and the mayor's comments; <a href="https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/2026/11/24/macys-parade-canceled-balloons-wind-noreaster/92938791007/">NorthJersey.com</a> for the wind limits and the NBC replay; <a href="https://www.wvlt.tv/2026/11/26/severe-weather-across-us-expected-complicate-thanksgiving-travel/">WVLT</a> for the power outages and flight disruption.</p>

<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>

<h3>When is the Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade now?</h3>
<p>Saturday 28th November 2026 at 8.30am ET in New York City (postponed from Thanksgiving Day, Thursday 26 November, because of the storm).</p>

<h3>Has the Macy's parade ever been put off before?</h3>
<p>No, it was cancelled from 1942 to 1944 during the Second World War, though 2026 is the first time it's been put off due to weather.</p>

<h3>Where can I catch the parade that's been rescheduled?</h3>
<p>NBC will broadcast it live on Saturday from 8.30 am ET, and it will also stream on Peacock and air on Telemundo.</p>
