-- raheem-sterling-suspended-sentence-driving-20261127 (news; UK; verifiedAt NULL)
INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt", "verifiedAt", "authorName")
VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'raheem-sterling-suspended-sentence-driving-20261127', 'news', 'UK',
'Raheem Sterling given suspended sentence for driving',
'Raheem Sterling given suspended sentence for driving',
'Raheem Sterling was given a 12-month suspended jail sentence on 25 November for dangerous driving after inhaling laughing gas before crashing his Lamborghini.',
'Raheem Sterling was given a 12-month suspended jail sentence on 25 November for dangerous driving after inhaling laughing gas before crashing his Lamborghini.',
$$<p>Former England winger Raheem Sterling was given a 12-month suspended jail sentence on Wednesday 25 November for dangerous driving, after he admitted inhaling laughing gas while behind the wheel before crashing his Lamborghini.</p>

<table>
<tr><td>Player</td><td>Raheem Sterling, 31, former England international</td></tr>
<tr><td>Court</td><td>Basingstoke Magistrates' Court</td></tr>
<tr><td>Sentence</td><td>12 months' imprisonment, suspended for 18 months</td></tr>
<tr><td>Other orders</td><td>100 hours' unpaid work; two-year driving ban</td></tr>
<tr><td>Incident</td><td>28 May 2026, M25 and M3 motorways</td></tr>
<tr><td>Plea</td><td>Guilty, 15 September 2026</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>What happened</h2>

<p>Sterling was reported to be driving erratically on the M25 and M3 motorways in south England during the morning rush hour on 28 May with witnesses stating he was inhaling from a balloon and weaving between lanes, according to <a href="https://www.aljazeera.com/amp/sports/2026/11/25/ex-england-star-sterling-given-suspended-sentence-for-dangerous-driving">Al Jazeera</a>. Dashcam footage showed him nearly hitting the central reservation on the M3 before he crashed his Lamborghini Urus. He made no reaction at all when the sentence was passed.</p>

<p>Judge Kirsty Allman said Sterling had been acting with a conscious disregard for the safety of other road users. 12 months' imprisonment suspended for 18 months, 100 hours of unpaid work, <a href="https://www.skysports.com/football/news/13616290/raheem-sterling-former-england-international-given-suspended-12-month-jail-sentence-for-dangerous-driving">Sky Sports</a> reported. He was also disqualified from driving ban with a requirement to retake the test to get his licence.</p>

<p>Sterling, who won four Premier League titles with Manchester City and made 82 appearances for England, pleaded guilty in September to dangerous driving, possession of six nitrous oxide canisters (for wrongful inhalation), a class C drug and failing to provide a specimen, according to <a href="https://www.arabnews.com/football/soccer-star-sterling-gets-suspended-jail-sentence-for-dangerous-driving-while-inhaling-from-balloon-3013999">Arab News</a>. He most recently played for Dutch side Feyenoord.</p>

<h2>What the Raheem Sterling sentence means</h2>

<p>The suspended sentence means Sterling won't go to prison (unless he commits another offence during the 18 month suspension period). The two year driving ban and the order to do unpaid work are both immediate and are public. It's also a case which serves as a warning about nitrous oxide (laughing gas) which is a class C drug when possessed for the purpose of inhaling it and the dangers of using it whilst driving on a busy motorway at rush hour.</p>

<p>For Sterling's career it's a very difficult moment. At 31 and having spent a season in the Netherlands with Feyenoord he's no longer the first choice England winger that he was at Man City. A criminal conviction for dangerous driving will obviously follow him into any future contract discussions. The court heard no evidence of any other injuries as a result of the crash (that would have been to his detriment) and he accepted the guilty plea. More on the UK in our <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/uk-hospitality-100000-roles-neet-youth-pledge-20261018">UK hospitality jobs pledge</a> report and the wider world in our <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles">News</a> section.</p>

<h2>What the sources do not say</h2>

<p>None of the sources say whether Sterling will be appealing the sentence or whether he's made any comment at all since it was handed down. Nothing at all is known about what will happen to his footballing career, or whether Feyenoord or any other club have commented. There's no information as to whether any other road user was injured or whether any other vehicle was damaged in the crash.</p>

<p>Sources: <a href="https://www.skysports.com/football/news/13616290/raheem-sterling-former-england-international-given-suspended-12-month-jail-sentence-for-dangerous-driving">Sky Sports</a> for the sentence, the ban and the guilty plea; <a href="https://www.aljazeera.com/amp/sports/2026/11/25/ex-england-star-sterling-given-suspended-sentence-for-dangerous-driving">Al Jazeera</a> for the judge's comments and the 'erratic' driving; <a href="https://www.arabnews.com/football/soccer-star-sterling-gets-suspended-jail-sentence-for-dangerous-driving-while-inhaling-from-balloon-3013999">Arab News</a> for the charges and the details of the crash.</p>

<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>

<h3>What sentence did Raheem Sterling get?</h3>
<p>A 12 month prison sentence (suspended for 18 months), 100 hours of unpaid work and a two year driving ban. He'll have to retake his driving test.</p>

<h3>What did Sterling plead guilty to?</h3>
<p>Dangerous driving, possession of six nitrous oxide canisters for wrongful inhalation and failure to provide a specimen following a crash involving his Lamborghini Urus on 28 May 2026.</p>

<h3>Will Sterling go to prison?</h3>
<p>Not unless he commits another offence during the 18 month suspension period. The sentence is suspended so he's at large whilst the orders are in force.</p>
