(gen_random_uuid(), 'trump-giuliani-medal-of-freedom-20261127', 'news', 'USA',
'Trump awards Giuliani the Medal of Freedom',
'Trump awards Giuliani the Medal of Freedom',
'Donald Trump awarded Rudy Giuliani the Presidential Medal of Freedom on 24 November, honouring the former New York mayor for his 9/11 leadership.',
'Donald Trump awarded Rudy Giuliani the Presidential Medal of Freedom on 24 November, honouring the former New York mayor for his 9/11 leadership.',
$$<p>President Trump awarded Rudy Giuliani the Presidential Medal of Freedom (the highest civilian honour in the country) in a private Oval Office ceremony on Tuesday 24th November.</p>

<table>
<tr><td>Recipient</td><td>Rudy Giuliani, former New York mayor, aged 82</td></tr>
<tr><td>Award</td><td>Presidential Medal of Freedom</td></tr>
<tr><td>Date</td><td>Tuesday 24 November 2026</td></tr>
<tr><td>Presented by</td><td>President Donald Trump, Oval Office</td></tr>
<tr><td>Announced</td><td>1 September 2025</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>What happened</h2>

<p>Trump personally fastened the medal round Giuliani's neck at the private ceremony, according to the <a href="https://nypost.com/2026/11/24/us-news/trump-to-honor-americas-mayor-rudy-giuliani-with-the-presidential-medal-of-freedom/">New York Post</a>. Giuliani, 'America's Mayor' as he was known for his leadership in the aftermath of the 11 September 2001 attacks, is only the third person Trump has bestowed the medal upon in his second term (Charlie Kirk and Welles Crowther being the others). Giuliani said he was 'honoured and humbled' to receive the medal from the president, <a href="https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/2026/11/24/trump-rudy-giuliani-medal-freedom/92939924007/">USA Today</a> reported.</p>

<p>Trump had announced his intention to honour Giuliani on 1st September 2025, just days after the former mayor had been seriously injured in a car crash in New Hampshire. At the time Trump called him the greatest mayor New York City has ever had and an equally great American patriot, and said he would be awarded the nation's highest civilian honour. Giuliani (82) told Newsmax after the ceremony that it was very special to be honoured in that way, particularly given the friendship he shared with Trump and the fact that a portrait of Ronald Reagan (his former boss) was in the room.</p>

<p>The award also recognises Giuliani's earlier career as a federal prosecutor working on organised crime and his two terms as Mayor of New York. Trump has also announced that he will be awarding it to Ben Carson (former Housing Secretary), hockey goalie Connor Hellebuyck and baseball player Roger Clemens, according to USA Today.</p>

<h2>What the Giuliani Medal of Freedom means</h2>

<p>The medal is the highest civilian honour that can be bestowed by the White House and it's one of Trump's most personal awards, honouring a man who has been his lawyer, his ally and his friend for decades. Giuliani was the man who led New York through the 11 September attacks and that's the very essence of the citation despite the fact that his subsequent career has been extremely controversial. The <a href="https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3375672/trump-awards-rudy-giuliani-medal-freedom-highest-us-civilian-honour">South China Morning Post</a> pointed out that Giuliani subsequently assisted Trump in his efforts to overturn the 2020 election result, was disbarred and was criminally indicted and was then granted a full pardon by Trump last year.</p>

<p>The private nature of the ceremony also matters. Unlike some Medal of Freedom presentations, which are public events with speeches and guests, this one was held behind closed doors in the Oval Office, with photographs released afterwards. That choice fits a pattern in Trump's second term of using the medal to honour allies and figures from his own political movement, including Kirk, who was killed earlier this year. More on the Trump White House in our <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/trump-tariffs-china-eu-20261125">Trump tariffs plan for China and the EU</a> and the wider world news is in our <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles">News</a> section.</p>

<h2>What the sources do not say</h2>

<p>None of the sources give the full text of the citation or state who else was at the private ceremony. They don't say when the medals for Ben Carson, Connor Hellebuyck and Roger Clemens will be presented (or indeed if those ceremonies will be public). There's no mention of whether Giuliani will be taking on any formal role as a result of the honour.</p>

<p>Sources: <a href="https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/2026/11/24/trump-rudy-giuliani-medal-freedom/92939924007/">USA Today</a> for the ceremony and Giuliani's statement; <a href="https://nypost.com/2026/11/24/us-news/trump-to-honor-americas-mayor-rudy-giuliani-with-the-presidential-medal-of-freedom/">New York Post</a> for the Oval Office detail and the September 2025 announcement; <a href="https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3375672/trump-awards-rudy-giuliani-medal-freedom-highest-us-civilian-honour">South China Morning Post</a> for the background on the 2020 election and the pardon; <a href="https://www.nst.com.my/world/world/2026/11/1585185/trump-awards-rudy-giuliani-top-civilian-honour?source=widget">New Straits Times</a> for the award as the nation's top civilian honour.</p>

<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>

<h3>What is the Presidential Medal of Freedom?</h3>
<p>It's the highest civilian honour in the US, awarded by the President to individuals who have made exceptional contributions to the security or national interests of the US, to world peace or to culture.</p>

<h3>Why did Trump give the medal to Rudy Giuliani?</h3>
<p>For his leadership as mayor of New York after the 11 September 2001 attacks and his decades of public service, including his work as a federal prosecutor against organised crime.</p>

<h3>Who else has Trump given the medal to in his second term?</h3>
<p>Charlie Kirk and Welles Crowther got it before Giuliani. Trump has also announced the award to Ben Carson, Connor Hellebuyck and Roger Clemens.</p>
