INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt", "verifiedAt", "authorName")
VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'bigbang-giiirip-surprise-single-milkshake-20261127', 'pop-music', 'Korea',
'BIGBANG GiiiRIP Surprise Single Spins Kelis Milkshake',
'BIGBANG GiiiRIP Surprise Single Spins Kelis Milkshake',
'BIGBANG GiiiRIP is a surprise single built on Kelis'' Milkshake, as the trio''s 20th anniversary year rolls on with a world tour and a new film.',
'BIGBANG GiiiRIP is a surprise single built on Kelis'' Milkshake, as the trio''s 20th anniversary year rolls on with a world tour and a new film.',
$$<p>BIGBANG GiiiRIP arrived as a surprise digital single on Friday 20th November (the K-pop group's second new song in three months as their 20th anniversary year continues). It's an electronic hip-hop track based on an interpolation of Kelis' 2003 hit 'Milkshake' and the title comes from the Korean word for standing up.</p>

<table>
<tr><td>Song</td><td>"GiiiRIP" — BIGBANG</td></tr>
<tr><td>Released</td><td>20 November 2026, 2pm Korea time</td></tr>
<tr><td>Sound</td><td>Electronic hip-hop, built on Kelis' "Milkshake"</td></tr>
<tr><td>Title meaning</td><td>Korean "girip" — to stand up, a standing ovation</td></tr>
<tr><td>Members</td><td>G-Dragon, Taeyang, Daesung</td></tr>
<tr><td>Writers</td><td>G-Dragon, Taeyang, TEDDY, with Pharrell Williams and Chad Hugo</td></tr>
<tr><td>First performance</td><td>2026 MAMA Awards, 21 November, Kyocera Dome Osaka</td></tr>
<tr><td>Visual film</td><td>Released 25 November 2026</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>What happened</h2>

<p>YG announced the single with just a handful of hours of teaser promotion (three black and white close ups, one for each member) before 'GiiiRIP' went up on all the streaming services at 2pm Korea time on 20th November (according to <a href="https://www.bandwagon.asia/articles/bigbang-put-their-spin-on-kelis-milkshake-with-surprise-single-giiirip">Bandwagon</a>). The concept is a standing ovation really: after two decades on stage they're singing as if the crowd is already on their feet. G-Dragon co-wrote the lyrics and the music, Taeyang did the lyrics and TEDDY did the track with Dan Dare, Jumpa and Alexander Tidebrink. Because the writers of that (Pharrell Williams and Chad Hugo of The Neptunes) are also credited.</p>

<p>The single follows 'BiiiG' which was released in August and marked BIGBANG's return to music as a group for the first time since 2022. The group that's returned is a trio (G-Dragon, Taeyang and Daesung) rather than the five piece that made the name. 'BiiiG' shot to No.1 on both Melon's Top 100 and Hot 100 within an hour of its release. 'GiiiRIP' got its first live performance the day after release at Chapter 2 of the 2026 MAMA Awards at the Kyocera Dome Osaka on 21st November and the performance video on Mnet's official YouTube channel racked up 4.75 million views (the most of any video from the two days of the show). A first official music video for the song came out on 25th November, shot almost entirely in black and white with the trio performing alongside dozens of dancers. The Japan leg of the group's XX: COSMOS world tour (41 shows across 20 cities) kicks off on 27th November. Our report on the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/bigbang-surprise-digital-single-november-20-20261121">initial news of BIGBANG's surprise single</a> covered the release itself and the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/popmusic">Pop Music</a> hub has the rest of the week's K-pop news.</p>

<h2>What the BIGBANG GiiiRIP release means</h2>

<p>Two singles in three months, a world tour and a MAMA performance all add up to more than just an anniversary lap. Having gone over four years without new music prior to' Biiig', the question was whether one song would be a rather token nostalgic piece. ' GiiiRIP' is the answer to that at least for now: the group is releasing again, and the "Milkshake" interpolation is a deliberate bridge between the trio's club-ready present and a pop touchstone from the early 2000s. The styling of the title is also telling in that the three lower case' i's mirror' BiiiG' and stand for the three active members. An album is still missing though. YG has not announced a title or a date for the album which is expected to contain the two singles, though it's reported that one will be released next year.</p>

<h2>What the sources do not say</h2>

<p>There's nothing in the report as to a chart position for "GiiiRIP" on the Billboard charts or a first week streaming number so we don't know at this stage what its commercial performance is going to be outside of Korea. No mention is not yet stated. The sources do not say whether an album compiling "BiiiG" and "GiiiRIP" will have a title or a release date, nor do they confirm that the group will continue to release new music once the 20th anniversary festivities are over. They don't say anything about "GiiiRIP" being performed on the Japan leg of the tour either.</p>

<p>Sources: <a href="https://www.bandwagon.asia/articles/bigbang-put-their-spin-on-kelis-milkshake-with-surprise-single-giiirip">Bandwagon</a> for the release, the 'Milkshake' interpolation and the tour; <a href="https://www.abs-cbn.com/entertainment/showbiz/music/2026/11/21/bigbang-inspires-self-assurance-with-energetic-new-single-giiirip-1239">ABS-CBN</a> for the YG statement and the writing credits; <a href="https://asiadaily.org/news/20399/">Asia Daily</a> for the visual film and the release timeline; <a href="https://www.martincid.com/music-en/bigbang-giiirip/">Martin Cid Magazine</a> for the title meaning, the 'BiiiG' comparison and the album outlook.</p>

<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
<h3>What does GiiiRIP mean?</h3>
<p>It's derived from the Korean word 'girip' which means 'to stand up' or a standing ovation. The three lowercase 'i's are a reference to the styling of 'BiiiG' and of course represent the three active members of the group.</p>
<h3>What song does BIGBANG's GiiiRIP sample?</h3>
<p>It interpolates Kelis' 'Milkshake' (2003) which was written by Pharrell Williams and Chad Hugo (both of whom are credited on the new track).</p>
<h3>When was BIGBANG's GiiiRIP released?</h3>
<p>As a surprise digital single on 20 November 2026 (three months after 'BiiiG'). Its first live performance was at the 2026 MAMA Awards on 21 November and a visual film followed on 25 November.</p>
