$$<p>Karol G BbY WOW is back at No.1 on the Billboard Global 200, back to the top of the worldwide singles chart for a seventh nonconsecutive week. The Karol G x Judeline x rusowsky collaboration also extends its run at No.1 on the Billboard Global Excl. US chart to eight weeks.</p>

<table>
<tr><td>Song</td><td>"BbY WOW" — Karol G, Judeline and rusowsky</td></tr>
<tr><td>Billboard Global 200</td><td>No. 1, seventh week at the top</td></tr>
<tr><td>Global Excl. US</td><td>No. 1, eighth week at the top</td></tr>
<tr><td>Global streams</td><td>36.5 million in the tracking week</td></tr>
<tr><td>Streams outside the US</td><td>29.8 million</td></tr>
<tr><td>Tracking week</td><td>13–19 November 2026</td></tr>
<tr><td>Chart dated</td><td>28 November 2026</td></tr>
<tr><td>First reached No. 1</td><td>Mid-September 2026</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>What happened</h2>

<p>According to Billboard's chart report, published on Monday, 23 November, "BbY WOW" climbed back to No. 1 on the Global 200 on 36.5 million streams worldwide in the 13–19 November tracking week, including 29.8 million streams outside the United States, <a href="https://www.musictimes.com/articles/113387/20261125/karol-gs-bby-wow-spends-seventh-week-no-1-christmas-songs-return.htm">MusicTimes</a> reported. The song first reached No. 1 on both global charts in mid-September, and this is its seventh total week at the summit of the Global 200.</p>

<p>The rest of the top five really does highlight just how crowded the global chart is. Ashe's "Stop the Wedding" is at No.2, Tate McRae's "Housewife" at No.3. The Christmas charts have arrived early with Wham!'s "Last Christmas" at No.4 and Mariah Carey's "All I Want for Christmas Is You" at No.5 on the 28 November chart. The Global 200 and Global Excl. US charts are compiled from streaming and digital sales across over 200 territories (the latter of course excluding US consumption). Our report on <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/ashe-stop-the-wedding-spotify-global-number-one-20261124">Ashe's Stop the Wedding taking the top spot on Spotify's global chart</a> covered the song now edging Karol G, and the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/popmusic">Pop Music</a> hub has the rest of the chart news from the week.</p>

<h2>What the Karol G BbY WOW return means</h2>

<p>Seven weeks at No.1 over two months is a very different kind of hit to a song that debuts at the top and then just fades. "BbY WOW" is coming back and that return is significant as it's effectively holding off the new crop of chart entries from Ashe and Tate McRae and the two biggest Christmas songs of the modern day (both of which have been climbing for weeks prior to December). The strength of the song internationally is the real story with 29.8m of its 36.5m streams coming from outside the US and its eighth week at the top of the Global Excl. US chart proving that this is a global hit first and an American hit second. With the Christmas songs still on the rise, the next chart is going to be the first real test of whether Karol G can actually keep the top spot into December.</p>

<h2>What the sources do not say</h2>

<p>There's nothing in the coverage to indicate a Hot 100 position for "BbY WOW" in the US, so we don't have any information on the song's performance in its home market. It's not stated. The sources do not say whether Karol G, Judeline or rusowsky have any new release, video or performance planned around the chart return. There's no breakdown of the streams by country or platform and no information on how the total weeks at No.1 stack up against Karol G's previous global chart runs.</p>

<p>Sources: <a href="https://www.musictimes.com/articles/113387/20261125/karol-gs-bby-wow-spends-seventh-week-no-1-christmas-songs-return.htm">MusicTimes</a> for the chart positions, the stream numbers and the tracking week; <a href="https://www.power106.com/2026/11/24/karol-g-returns-to-no-1-on-the-global-charts-for-a-seventh-week/">Power 106</a> for the seventh week return; <a href="https://www.rockumweb.com/reportes/2845/karol-g-returns-to-no-1-on-billboard-global-200-as-wham-and-mariah-carey-surge-into-top-5-for-christmas">Rockumweb</a> for the top-five order and the chart methodology.</p>

<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
<h3>How many weeks has Karol G's BbY WOW been at No.1 on the Global 200?</h3>
<p>Seven non-consecutive weeks (including its return to the top on the chart dated 28th November 2026). It's also spent eight weeks at No.1 on the Billboard Global Excl. US chart.</p>
<h3>Who are the artists on BbY WOW?</h3>
<p>Karol G, Judeline and rusowsky. The song first reached No. 1 on both Billboard global charts in mid-September 2026.</p>
<h3>What is the Billboard Global 200?</h3>
<p>A weekly worldwide singles chart compiled from streaming and digital song sales across more than 200 markets. Its sister chart, Global Excl. US, omits the US.</p>
