(gen_random_uuid(), 'miss-universe-2026-winner-jennifer-barreto-20261127', 'pop-music', 'Global',
'Miss Universe 2026 Winner Jennifer Barreto Makes History',
'Miss Universe 2026 Winner Jennifer Barreto Makes History',
'Miss Universe 2026 winner Jennifer Barreto of Puerto Rico is the first married mother to take the crown, at the pageant''s 75th edition in San Juan.',
'Miss Universe 2026 winner Jennifer Barreto of Puerto Rico is the first married mother to take the crown, at the pageant''s 75th edition in San Juan.',
$$<p>Miss Universe 2026 winner Jennifer Barreto of Puerto Rico was crowned on home soil on Tuesday, 24 November, becoming the first married woman and mother ever to win the title. The 27 year old psychologist and social worker triumphed over 115 other contestants at the Jose Miguel Agrelot Coliseum in San Juan during the 75th edition.</p>

<table>
<tr><td>Winner</td><td>Jennifer Barreto, Puerto Rico, 27</td></tr>
<tr><td>Profession</td><td>Psychologist and social worker</td></tr>
<tr><td>Finale</td><td>24 November 2026, Jose Miguel Agrelot Coliseum, San Juan</td></tr>
<tr><td>Edition</td><td>75th Miss Universe</td></tr>
<tr><td>Contestants</td><td>116 countries and territories</td></tr>
<tr><td>1st runner-up</td><td>Melissa Nunez, Dominican Republic</td></tr>
<tr><td>2nd runner-up</td><td>Clara Vegas, Venezuela</td></tr>
<tr><td>3rd runner-up</td><td>Bea Millan-Windorski, Philippines</td></tr>
<tr><td>4th runner-up</td><td>Georgia Waddington, New Zealand</td></tr>
<tr><td>Crown</td><td>"The Radiance of an Eternal Legacy", 3,150 diamonds</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>What happened</h2>

<p>Barreto was crowned by outgoing titleholder Fatima Bosch of Mexico (who won in 2025) in front of a home crowd in San Juan. The hosts were Mario Lopez and former Miss Universe R'Bonney Gabriel (according to <a href="https://www.cnn.com/2026/11/25/style/miss-universe-2026-winner?cid=external-feeds_iluminar_meta">CNN</a>. The final five faced judges' questions on topics including what the world needs from its leaders. Barreto's answer on the subject of human values in the age of AI was the one that clinched it for her. She said that technology should be used responsibly and that the real values of a person are in the consistency between what they say and what they do, particularly when that consistency is difficult to achieve.</p>

<p>The result is a piece of pageant history. Barreto is the first mother and the first married woman to win Miss Universe since organisers lifted the ban on contestants who had ever married or given birth three years ago, <a href="https://www.cnn.com/2026/11/25/style/miss-universe-2026-winner?cid=external-feeds_iluminar_meta">CNN</a> reported. Her win is Puerto Rico's sixth Miss Universe title, its first since Zuleyka Rivera in 2006, and only the United States and Venezuela have won more. The new crown, "The Radiance of an Eternal Legacy", was designed by Venezuelan jeweller George Wittels with 3,150 diamonds set in 18-karat white gold, according to <a href="https://people.com/miss-universe-2026-winner-jennifer-barreto-12267491">People</a>. The runner-up order was confirmed by <a href="https://www.philstar.com/lifestyle/fashion-and-beauty/2026/11/25/2572560/miss-universe-2026-puerto-ricos-jennifer-barreto-phs-bea-millan-windorski-3rd-runner-up">Philstar</a>: Melissa Nunez of the Dominican Republic first, Clara Vegas of Venezuela second, Bea Millan-Windorski of the Philippines third and Georgia Waddington of New Zealand fourth. Our preview of the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/miss-universe-2026-finale-november-24-preview-20261123">Miss Universe 2026 finale</a> set out what was at stake before the night, and the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/popmusic">Pop Music</a> hub has the rest of the week's entertainment news.</p>

<p>The final itself went pretty smoothly, the build up was a mess though. A number of delegates dropped out prior to the final due to visa delays, including the delegate from Nepal and five African countries, including first time entrants South Sudan and the Republic of Congo). Six delegates from the Southeast Asian region (Indonesia, Laos, Malaysia, Singapore, Thailand and Vietnam) were also absent following a contractual dispute between the Miss Universe Organisation and the Thai businessman who runs the qualifying pageants in that region. The Miss Universe France organisers also pulled their delegate in protest at the 2025 final and a replacement in the form of Garance Authie was appointed who made it to the Top 12.</p>

<h2>What the Miss Universe 2026 winner means</h2>

<p>This win changes the complexion of what a Miss Universe winner can be. For the majority of the pageant's 75 year history married women and mothers were simply not allowed at all; Barreto's win three years after the ban was lifted is the first tangible proof that the rule change was anything other than a mere formality. It's also significant in the context of where it happened: Puerto Rico has hosted the final on four occasions and a home winner in the Diamond Jubilee year gives the organisation after a year in which it has been under a microscope for vote rigging allegations surrounding the 2025 result (a jury was only revealed the day before the final) and with no independent auditor having been involved for three years. Whether that goodwill will be sustained will depend on the extent to which the organisation can answer the transparency questions that its critics have been asking all along (who are the judges, how are they selected and how are the scores verified).</p>

<h2>What the sources do not say</h2>

<p>Nothing in the report states what Barreto's initial duties as Miss Universe will be, or where her first year as Miss Universe will take her. The sources give no details on the judges' scores or on the ranking of the final five beyond the order in which they were announced. They don't say whether the absent Southeast Asian delegates will be back next year (the pageant director in question does hope they can be). They don't say how the organisation plans to resolve its dispute with that director, nor do they say whether an independent auditor will be brought back for 2027.</p>

<p>Sources: <a href="https://www.cnn.com/2026/11/25/style/miss-universe-2026-winner?cid=external-feeds_iluminar_meta">CNN</a> for the result, the venue, the history-making win, and the controversies; <a href="https://www.philstar.com/lifestyle/fashion-and-beauty/2026/11/25/2572560/miss-universe-2026-puerto-ricos-jennifer-barreto-phs-bea-millan-windorski-3rd-runner-up">Philstar</a> for the sixth title and the full runner-up order; <a href="https://entertainment.inquirer.net/691481/jennifer-barreto-from-puerto-rico-crowned-miss-universe-2026-in-puerto-rico/amp">Inquirer</a> for the venue, the 75th edition, and the first mother and married winner; <a href="https://people.com/miss-universe-2026-winner-jennifer-barreto-12267491">People</a> for the crown details and Barreto's background.</p>

<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
<h3>Who won Miss Universe 2026?</h3>
<p>Jennifer Barreto (27, psychologist and social worker from Puerto Rico) was crowned on 24 November 2026 at the Jose Miguel Agrelot Coliseum in San Juan.</p>
<h3>Why is Jennifer Barreto's win historic?</h3>
<p>She is the first married woman and the first mother ever to win Miss Universe, three years after organisers lifted the ban on married women and mothers competing. It is also Puerto Rico's sixth title, its first since 2006.</p>
<h3>Who were the runners up at Miss Universe 2026?</h3>
<p>Melissa Nunez of the Dominican Republic was first runner-up, followed by Clara Vegas of Venezuela, Bea Millan-Windorski of the Philippines and Georgia Waddington of New Zealand.</p>
