INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt", "verifiedAt", "authorName")
VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'chatgpt-health-android-rollout-20261127', 'tech-ai', 'USA',
'ChatGPT Health reaches Android with Health Connect link',
'ChatGPT Health reaches Android with Health Connect link',
'ChatGPT Health Android rollout brings Health Connect support, letting US users link wearables so ChatGPT can read sleep and activity patterns.',
'ChatGPT Health Android rollout brings Health Connect support, letting US users link wearables so ChatGPT can read sleep and activity patterns.',
$$<p>OpenAI has now brought ChatGPT Health to Android, enabling users to connect their fitness apps and wearables via Google's Health Connect so that ChatGPT can read their sleep, exercise and activity data. The expansion, announced in OpenAI's release notes on 19 November 2026, also reaches the Mac desktop app, the Dots assistant and ChatGPT Sites.</p>

<table>
<tr><td>Company</td><td>OpenAI</td></tr>
<tr><td>Feature</td><td>ChatGPT Health</td></tr>
<tr><td>Android link</td><td>Health Connect, including Garmin, Oura and WHOOP</td></tr>
<tr><td>Availability</td><td>United States only; Free, Go, Plus and Pro; aged 18 and over</td></tr>
<tr><td>Rollout</td><td>From 19 November 2026, gradual</td></tr>
<tr><td>Also added</td><td>Mac desktop app, Dots proactive assistant, ChatGPT Sites</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>What happened</h2>

<p>ChatGPT Health launched in July 2026 on the web and on iOS where it connects to Apple Health and medical records. It expanded to Android on 19 November, where users connect their health and fitness information through Health Connect, Google's hub for health data. According to <a href="https://www.gadgets360.com/ai/news/openai-brings-chatgpt-health-to-android-lets-users-connect-wearables-fitness-apps-12379196">Gadgets360</a>, Android users can link in devices and services from Garmin, Oura and WHOOP (as long as they share the relevant data with Health Connect) and ChatGPT will then be able to help them interpret patterns in their sleep, activity and other wellness data.</p>

<p>To get going, users update the ChatGPT app, go to Health either from the sidebar or the Explore menu, select Health Connect and then pick the data categories you'd like to share. OpenAI notes the Android rollout is gradual so the Health section may not be available to all users immediately. The feature is available to eligible logged in users on Free, Go, Plus and Pro plans (us only) and users must be 18+ to use it.</p>

<p>The expansion also includes health data in Dots (OpenAI's proactive assistant) which can now provide reminders and suggestions based on the health data that's connected to the user. So if a meeting comes up and it's going to interfere with a workout, Dots can suggest an alternative time for the workout. It can also provide a reminder around preventative care based on the health data that's connected. Users can also build a site based on their health data via the ChatGPT desktop app.</p>

<p>Same day OpenAI updated its Health Privacy Notice. From 19th November chats that use connected health data may be used to improve OpenAI's models depending on the user's settings (this reverses the previous blanket exclusion), according to <a href="https://aiweekly.co/alerts/openai-expands-chatgpt-health-to-mac-android-dots-sites">AI Weekly</a> who are reporting on the 9to5Mac piece. The actual connected health data itself is not used to train the foundation models. A chat that references connected health data can go into training though, provided the user has not turned off the model improvement setting in Data Controls.</p>

<h2>What the ChatGPT Health Android rollout means</h2>

<p>This is the moment ChatGPT Health stops being an Apple only thing. Android is the bigger phone platform in the world and Health Connect is the way in. Rather than go in and build their own wearable integrations they're just going to read whatever the user's tracker is syncing into the Google hub. For the user that means their sleep, steps and workouts from a Garmin watch or an Oura ring can now be alongside their medical records in the same conversation and the assistant can look for patterns across them (e.g. poor sleep following late workouts).</p>

<p>The privacy change is just as important as the platform change. Health was launched with the explicit promise that health conversations would not be used to train the models and that promise was quietly dropped on the very same day the feature expanded. The opt-out is there, but it's a setting you have to go and find and turn off. The default is now to allow health conversations to be used to improve the default now lets health-linked chats feed model improvement. Anyone who's got a wearable should check their Data Controls. The US only restriction remains (no date for other countries). More on OpenAI's health work is in our <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/openai-chatgpt-healthcare-computer-use-agents-20261118">ChatGPT healthcare coverage</a> and the wider picture is in our <a href="https://growentix.cloud/tech-ai">Tech news</a> section.</p>

<h2>What the sources do not say</h2>

<p>The sources do not say when ChatGPT Health will reach users outside the United States, or whether the Android rollout will extend to the Go plan in every region where it is offered. OpenAI has not said how long the gradual rollout will take, or what share of Android users can already see the Health section. The sources do not say exactly which data categories Health Connect shares by default, or how long OpenAI keeps synced health records. The sources do not say whether Dots' access to health information requires a particular plan, and OpenAI has not published a list of every wearable brand that works through Health Connect beyond the examples given.</p>

<p>Sources: <a href="https://www.gadgets360.com/ai/news/openai-brings-chatgpt-health-to-android-lets-users-connect-wearables-fitness-apps-12379196">Gadgets360</a> for the Android rollout, the Health Connect link, the Garmin, Oura and WHOOP examples, the US only limit and the gradual rollout; <a href="https://aiweekly.co/alerts/openai-expands-chatgpt-health-to-mac-android-dots-sites">AI Weekly</a> for the 19th November Health Privacy Notice change and the training opt-out; <a href="https://www.neowin.net/news/openai-is-giving-the-chatgpt-mobile-app-a-major-redesign/">Neowin</a> for the 19th November release notes, the Dots suggestions and the July 2026 launch.</p>

<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>

<h3>How do I connect ChatGPT Health on Android?</h3>
<p>Update the ChatGPT app, go to Health either from the sidebar or the Explore menu, select Health Connect and then pick which data categories you'd like to share. The rollout is incremental so the Health section may not be visible to everyone at the moment and it's only available in the US at this stage.</p>

<h3>Will my health chats train OpenAI's models?</h3>
<p>They can. Since 19th November 2026 chats which leverage connected health data can be used to improve OpenAI's models (unless you turn off the model improvement setting in Data Controls). The connected health data itself is not used to train the foundation models.</p>
