-- claude-duet-india-launch-20261127 (tech-ai; India; verifiedAt NULL)
INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt", "verifiedAt", "authorName")
VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'claude-duet-india-launch-20261127', 'tech-ai', 'India',
'Claude Duet reaches India with waitlist for paid users',
'Claude Duet reaches India with waitlist for paid users',
'Claude Duet India launch brings Anthropic''s proactive AI agent to paid users on a waitlist, with Team on public beta and Enterprise on private beta.',
'Claude Duet India launch brings Anthropic''s proactive AI agent to paid users on a waitlist, with Team on public beta and Enterprise on private beta.',
$$<p>Anthropic has expanded Claude Duet (its proactive AI agent) to India, opening the research preview to paid subscribers via a waitlist on Wednesday 25th November 2026. Team customers get the public beta and enterprise customers get the private beta a month after the agent launched in the United States.</p>

<table>
<tr><td>Company</td><td>Anthropic</td></tr>
<tr><td>Product</td><td>Claude Duet, proactive AI work agent</td></tr>
<tr><td>Model</td><td>Claude Opus 5.5</td></tr>
<tr><td>India access</td><td>Pro, Max and Ultra subscribers, by waitlist</td></tr>
<tr><td>Team</td><td>Public beta</td></tr>
<tr><td>Enterprise</td><td>Private beta</td></tr>
<tr><td>Platforms</td><td>Standalone app on iOS and Android, plus claude.ai</td></tr>
<tr><td>Languages</td><td>35, including Hindi, Bengali, Tamil and Telugu</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>What happened</h2>

<p>Anthropic have announced the expansion of the research preview of Claude Duet to India, with waitlist access for Pro, Max and Ultra users, a public beta for Team plans and a private beta for enterprises, according to the PTI report via <a href="https://www.telegraphindia.com/business/anthropic-brings-claude-duet-to-india-with-ai-that-works-when-devices-are-switched-off/cid/2191273">Telegraph India</a>. The app is available as a standalone app on iOS and Android as well as via claude.ai. The preview was also opened in Indonesia, Brazil and Japan on the same day, <a href="https://www.gadgets360.com/ai/news/claude-duet-ai-assistant-india-app-available-research-preview-12380234">Gadgets360</a> reported.</p>

<p>Claude Duet is built on top of Claude Opus 5.5 and is designed to be a proactive assistant rather than just sitting and waiting for you to tell it what to do. It's going to be watching your connected apps and will send you a very short morning summary of the key items across them. It will only message you when something requires your attention. It can schedule meetings, draft emails, track your unpaid invoices, build dashboards, create sales forecasts, build web apps and will keep going in the background even if your devices are switched off.</p>

<p>Anthropic said the app would be of particular interest to founders, business owners, consultants and small business operators in India who are constantly juggling emails, invoices, customer requests, hiring and meetings. It works in all 35 of the languages that Claude supports (including Hindi, Bengali, Marathi, Telugu, Tamil, Gujarati, Kannada, Malayalam, Bhojpuri and English). Eligible users in India can go on the Claude website to join the waitlist and Anthropic will email them when they're in.</p>

<p>Approval is still required for sensitive actions. Access is provided with approval required for sending messages, making payments and other sensitive actions, <a href="https://inc42.com/buzz/anthropic-takes-on-openai-meta-with-new-proactive-ai-agent-claude-duet/">Inc42</a> reported. Anthropic also cautions that as Claude Duet is still in research preview the agent can misread a thread or miscalibrate as to what is urgent.</p>

<h2>What the Claude Duet India launch means</h2>

<p>Claude Duet is a completely different beast to a chatbot in that it observes, it prioritises and it acts. That's also why Anthropic are launching it so slowly, behind a waitlist rather than just turning it on for all. An agent that can send messages, move money and work whilst your phone is away needs trust and the research preview is Anthropic's way of building that trust in stages, with user feedback at each stage informing the product as it evolves.</p>

<p>India is a purposeful second market rather than an afterthought. The 35 language support (including nine of the major Indian languages) and the targeting of founders and small business owners who are managing everything themselves is all very much geared towards the Indian market and its massive base of SMES and independent professionals. It's also a direct challenge to OpenAI, Google and Meta in the race to build assistants that will do work rather than just answer questions. The real question is how fast the waitlist will move. A waitlist launch will generate demand but the Indian users who signed up will be the ones to judge it on how quickly they actually get in. More on Anthropic's assistant work can be found in our <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/claude-sheets-whiteboards-interactive-connectors-20261115">Claude connectors coverage</a> and the broader field is covered in our <a href="https://growentix.cloud/tech-ai">Tech news</a> section.</p>

<h2>What the sources do not say</h2>

<p>The sources don't say how long the waitlist will take, how many Indian users will be taken on, or when Claude Duet will leave the research preview. They don't say what Claude Duet costs beyond the existing Pro, Max and Ultra subscriptions (whether there will ever be a free tier is also not clear). The sources don't say which apps Claude Duet will be able to connect to in India, nor do they say whether the Indian payment and messaging integrations will be any different from the US version. The sources don't say how Anthropic will handle the data from the apps that are connected to Duet, or for how long it will retain the information that Duet is reading in the background as it's working.</p>

<p>Sources: <a href="https://www.telegraphindia.com/business/anthropic-brings-claude-duet-to-india-with-ai-that-works-when-devices-are-switched-off/cid/2191273">Telegraph India</a>(carrying the PTI report) for the announcement, the access tiers, the Opus 5.5 model and the 35 languages; <a href="https://www.gadgets360.com/ai/news/claude-duet-ai-assistant-india-app-available-research-preview-12380234">Gadgets360</a> for the expansion to Indonesia, Brazil and Japan, the standalone app listings and the research preview caveat; <a href="https://inc42.com/buzz/anthropic-takes-on-openai-meta-with-new-proactive-ai-agent-claude-duet/">Inc42</a> for the US launch a month earlier and the requirement for approval on messages, payments and other sensitive actions.</p>

<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>

<h3>How do I get Claude Duet in India?</h3>
<p>Pro, Max and Ultra subscribers can go on the waitlist via the Claude website and will be emailed when they're admitted. Team customers get in via the public beta and enterprise customers via the private beta. The app is available on iOS, Android and the web.</p>

<h3>What can Claude Duet do whilst my device is switched off?</h3>
<p>It's working in the background across the connected apps, watching for anything that needs attention and preparing the associated items (briefings, dashboards, forecasts etc). It only messages you when something requires attention and you have to approve any messages it sends, any payments it makes and so on before it sends messages, makes payments or takes other sensitive actions.</p>
